1
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,402
[FEMALE WHISPERS IN ELVISH]

2
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:37,656
FEMALE VOICE:
<i>The world is changed.</i>

3
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:40,783
<i>I feel it in the water.</i>

4
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:44,454
<i>I feel it in the earth.</i>

5
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:49,038
<i>I smell it in the air.</i>

6
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,422
<i>Much that once was...</i>

7
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,125
<i>...is lost.</i>

8
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,841
<i>For none now live who remember it.</i>

9
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:14,147
<i>It began with the forging</i>
<i>of the Great Rings.</i>

10
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:16,364
<i>Three were given to the Elves:</i>

11
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:20,285
<i>Immortal, wisest and fairest</i>
<i>of all beings.</i>

12
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,413
<i>Seven to the Dwarf-lords:</i>

13
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:28,581
<i>Great miners and craftsmen</i>
<i>of the mountain halls.</i>

14
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:30,378
<i>And nine...</i>

15
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:33,582
<i>...nine rings were gifted</i>
<i>to the race of Men...</i>

16
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:37,545
<i>...who, above all else, desire power.</i>

17
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:43,888
<i>For within these rings was bound</i>
<i>the strength and will to govern each race.</i>

18
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:48,560
<i>But they were all of them deceived.</i>

19
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,899
<i>For another ring was made.</i>

20
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:55,316
<i>In the land of Mordor,</i>
<i>in the fires of Mount Doom...</i>

21
00:01:55,741 --> 00:02:00,280
<i>...the Dark Lord Sauron forged</i>
<i>in secret a Master Ring...</i>

22
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:02,531
<i>...to control all others.</i>

23
00:02:02,623 --> 00:02:06,707
<i>And into this Ring he poured</i>
<i>his cruelty, his malice...</i>

24
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:11,036
<i>...and his will to dominate all life.</i>

25
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:15,875
<i>One Ring to rule them all.</i>

26
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,460
<i>One by one...</i>

27
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:23,345
<i>...the Free Lands of Middle-earth</i>
<i>fell to the power of the Ring.</i>

28
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:26,518
<i>But there were some who resisted.</i>

29
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:31,724
<i>A Last Alliance of Men and Elves</i>
<i>marched against the armies of Mordor.</i>

30
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:36,482
<i>And on the slopes of Mount Doom, they</i>
<i>fought for the freedom of Middle-earth.</i>

31
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:50,909
[SPEAKS ELVISH]

32
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:09,428
<i>Victory was near.</i>

33
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:15,934
<i>But the power of the Ring...</i>

34
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,190
<i>...could not be undone.</i>

35
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:44,797
<i>It was in this moment...</i>

36
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:47,382
<i>...when all hope had faded...</i>

37
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:51,641
<i>...that Isildur, son of the king,</i>
<i>took up his father's sword.</i>

38
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:29,217
<i>Sauron, the enemy of the Free Peoples</i>
<i>of Middle-earth, was defeated.</i>

39
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:38,350
<i>The Ring passed to Isildur...</i>

40
00:04:38,445 --> 00:04:42,688
<i>...who had this one chance</i>
<i>to destroy evil forever.</i>

41
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,615
<i>But the hearts of Men...</i>

42
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:48,239
<i>...are easily corrupted.</i>

43
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:53,116
<i>And the Ring of Power</i>
<i>has a will of its own.</i>

44
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,934
<i>It betrayed Isildur...</i>

45
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,193
<i>...to his death.</i>

46
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:33,330
<i>And some things</i>
<i>that should not have been forgotten...</i>

47
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,782
<i>...were lost.</i>

48
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:38,914
<i>History became legend...</i>

49
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:41,121
<i>...legend became myth.</i>

50
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:44,174
<i>And for</i>
<i>two and a half thousand years...</i>

51
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:48,004
<i>...the Ring passed</i>
<i>out of all knowledge.</i>

52
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,473
<i>Until, when chance came...</i>

53
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,260
<i>...it ensnared a new bearer.</i>

54
00:05:56,606 --> 00:06:01,441
GOLLUM:
My precious.

55
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:04,277
FEMALE VOICE: <i>The Ring came</i>
<i>to the creature Gollum...</i>

56
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:08,323
<i>...who took it deep into the tunnels</i>
<i>of the Misty Mountains.</i>

57
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,485
<i>And there it consumed him.</i>

58
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,862
GOLLUM:
It came to me.

59
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:18,496
My own. My love. My own.

60
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:23,331
My precious.

61
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:30,462
FEMALE VOICE: <i>The Ring brought</i>
<i>to Gollum unnatural long life.</i>

62
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:34,516
<i>For 500 years it poisoned his mind.</i>

63
00:06:34,603 --> 00:06:39,313
<i>And in the gloom of Gollum's cave,</i>
<i>it waited.</i>

64
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:42,687
<i>Darkness crept back</i>
<i>into the forests of the world.</i>

65
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:45,856
<i>Rumor grew of a shadow in the East...</i>

66
00:06:45,947 --> 00:06:48,859
<i>...whispers of a nameless fear.</i>

67
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:52,363
<i>And the Ring of Power perceived...</i>

68
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:55,287
<i>...its time had now come.</i>

69
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,371
<i>It abandoned Gollum.</i>

70
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:05,540
<i>But something happened then</i>
<i>the Ring did not intend.</i>

71
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:11,048
<i>It was picked up by the most unlikely</i>
<i>creature imaginable.</i>

72
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:12,299
BILBO:
What's this?

73
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,926
FEMALE VOICE:
<i>A Hobbit.</i>

74
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:16,884
<i>Bilbo Baggins of the Shire.</i>

75
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,843
A ring.

76
00:07:18,939 --> 00:07:20,850
GOLLUM:
Lost!

77
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,148
My precious is lost!

78
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:29,570
FEMALE VOICE:
<i>For the time will soon come...</i>

79
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:34,989
<i>...when Hobbits will shape</i>
<i>the fortunes of all.</i>

80
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:42,868
BILBO:
The 22nd day of September...

81
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:44,203
...in the year 1400...

82
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,039
...by Shire-reckoning.

83
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:54,137
Bag End, Bagshot Row, Hobbiton,
Westfarthing...

84
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:56,927
...the Shire...

85
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:59,885
...Middle-earth.

86
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:07,859
The Third Age of this world.

87
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:23,409
<i>There and Back Again:</i>

88
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,827
<i>A Hobbit's Tale.</i>

89
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,459
By Bilbo Baggins.

90
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:36,463
Now...

91
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,174
...where to begin?

92
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,513
Ah, yes....

93
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:47,690
"Concerning...

94
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,522
...Hobbits."

95
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:55,240
<i>Hobbits have been living and farming</i>
<i>in the four Farthings of the Shire...</i>

96
00:08:55,326 --> 00:08:57,408
<i>...for many hundreds of years...</i>

97
00:08:57,495 --> 00:09:00,578
<i>...quite content to ignore</i>
<i>and be ignored...</i>

98
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:03,873
<i>...by the world of the Big Folk.</i>

99
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:09,921
<i>Middle-earth being, after all,</i>
<i>full of strange creatures beyond count...</i>

100
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:13,250
<i>...Hobbits must seem</i>
<i>of little importance...</i>

101
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:17,462
<i>...being neither renowned</i>
<i>as great warriors...</i>

102
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:21,800
<i>...nor counted among the very wise.</i>

103
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:25,770
[KNOCKING]

104
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,183
Frodo! Someone at the door.

105
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,940
<i>In fact, it has been remarked by some...</i>

106
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:37,658
<i>...that Hobbits' only real passion</i>
<i>is for food.</i>

107
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,235
<i>A rather unfair observation...</i>

108
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:44,073
<i>...as we have also developed a keen</i>
<i>interest in the brewing of ales...</i>

109
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:47,208
<i>...and the smoking of pipe-weed.</i>

110
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:50,537
<i>But where our hearts truly lie...</i>

111
00:09:50,632 --> 00:09:52,839
<i>...is in peace and quiet...</i>

112
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:55,717
<i>...and good, tilled earth.</i>

113
00:09:55,804 --> 00:10:01,049
<i>For all Hobbits share a love</i>
<i>of things that grow.</i>

114
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:08,681
<i>And, yes, no doubt to others,</i>
<i>our ways seem quaint.</i>

115
00:10:08,775 --> 00:10:14,020
<i>But today of all days,</i>
<i>it is brought home to me:</i>

116
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:20,484
<i>It is no bad thing</i>
<i>to celebrate a simple life.</i>

117
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,612
[KNOCKING]

118
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:27,870
Frodo, the door!

119
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:32,920
Sticklebacks. Where is that boy?

120
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,544
Frodo!

121
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:44,883
MALE VOICE:
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

122
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:48,929
[WAGON RUMBLES]

123
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:53,395
<i>And I must follow if I can</i>

124
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:58,488
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

125
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:02,279
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

126
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:07,364
<i>Now far ahead the road has gone</i>

127
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:11,789
<i>-And I must follow if I can</i>
-You're late.

128
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,879
A wizard is never late, Frodo Baggins.

129
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:24,301
Nor is he early. He arrives
precisely when he means to.

130
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,770
It's wonderful to see you, Gandalf!

131
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:46,328
You didn't think I'd miss
your Uncle Bilbo's birthday?

132
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:50,160
How is the old rascal?

133
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:54,286
I hear it's going to be a party
of special magnificence.

134
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,871
You know Bilbo.
He's got the whole place in an uproar.

135
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,048
Well, that should please him.

136
00:11:59,135 --> 00:12:01,000
Half the Shire's been invited.

137
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:03,920
And the rest of them are turning up
anyway.

138
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:10,427
BILBO:
<i>And so life in the Shire goes on...</i>

139
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:13,684
<i>...very much as it has</i>
<i>this past Age...</i>

140
00:12:13,775 --> 00:12:19,395
<i>...full of its own comings and goings,</i>
<i>with change coming slowly.</i>

141
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:21,445
<i>If it comes at all.</i>

142
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:26,192
<i>For things are made to endure</i>
<i>in the Shire...</i>

143
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:29,825
<i>...passing from one generation</i>
<i>to the next.</i>

144
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:35,248
<i>There's always been a Baggins</i>
<i>living here under the Hill...</i>

145
00:12:35,338 --> 00:12:36,703
<i>...in Bag End.</i>

146
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:42,342
And there always will be.

147
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:46,379
To tell you the truth,
Bilbo's been a bit odd lately.

148
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,011
I mean, more than usual.

149
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,976
He's taken to locking himself
in his study.

150
00:12:54,524 --> 00:12:58,688
<i>He spends hours poring over old maps</i>
<i>when he thinks I'm not looking.</i>

151
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:13,035
Where's it gone?

152
00:13:39,569 --> 00:13:41,901
He's up to something.

153
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,620
-All right, then. Keep your secrets.
-What?

154
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,493
But I know you have something
to do with it.

155
00:13:54,584 --> 00:13:55,824
Good gracious me.

156
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,250
Before you came along, we Bagginses
were very well thought of.

157
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,077
Indeed.

158
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,584
Never had any adventures
or did anything unexpected.

159
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:09,137
If you're referring to the incident
with the dragon, I was barely involved.

160
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:12,932
All I did was give your uncle
a little nudge out of the door.

161
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:17,103
Whatever you did, you've been officially
labeled a disturber of the peace.

162
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,430
Oh, really?

163
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,029
Gandalf! Gandalf!

164
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:30,609
[CHILDREN SHOUTING]

165
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,362
FEMALE HOBBIT 1:
Fireworks, Gandalf!

166
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,042
FEMALE HOBBIT 2: Gandalf!
MALE HOBBIT: Fireworks, Gandalf!

167
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,933
Gandalf?

168
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:04,601
-I'm glad you're back.
-So am I, dear boy.

169
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,815
So am I.

170
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,461
Whoa, whoa.

171
00:15:42,692 --> 00:15:44,228
BILBO:
No, thank you!

172
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:48,402
We don't want any more visitors,
well-wishers or distant relations!

173
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:52,027
And what about very old friends?

174
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,865
Gandalf?

175
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:01,078
-Bilbo Baggins.
-My dear Gandalf!

176
00:16:01,169 --> 00:16:06,380
Good to see you. 111 years old!
Who would believe it?

177
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,125
You haven't aged a day.

178
00:16:16,726 --> 00:16:18,762
Come on, come in!

179
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,344
Welcome, welcome.

180
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:25,060
Oh, here we are.

181
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:29,227
Tea? Or maybe something
a little stronger?

182
00:16:29,322 --> 00:16:33,235
I've got a few bottles
of the Old Winyard left. 1296.

183
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:37,410
Very good year. Almost as old as I am.

184
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:43,120
It was laid down by my father.
What say we open one, eh?

185
00:16:43,211 --> 00:16:45,918
Just tea, thank you.

186
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,124
Oh!

187
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:53,926
I was expecting you sometime
last week.

188
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:57,422
Not that it matters. You come and go as
you please. Always have and always will.

189
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:02,973
You caught me a bit unprepared. We've
only got cold chicken and a bit of pickle....

190
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:06,431
There's some cheese here.
No, that won't do.

191
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:10,605
We've got raspberry jam,
an apple tart....

192
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:15,319
But not much for afters.
Oh, no, we're all right.

193
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:18,276
I've just found some sponge cake.

194
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:22,538
I could make you some eggs
if you'd--

195
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,957
-Just tea, thank you.
-Oh, right.

196
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,498
-You don't mind if I eat, do you?
-No, not at all.

197
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,049
[KNOCKING]

198
00:17:34,136 --> 00:17:35,501
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!

199
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,211
I'm not at home!

200
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,845
It's the Sackville-Bagginses.

201
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:48,101
-I know you're in there!
-They're after the house.

202
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:51,358
They've never forgiven me
for living this long.

203
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:54,312
I've got to get away from these confounded
relatives, hanging on the bell all day...

204
00:17:54,407 --> 00:17:56,318
...never giving me a moment's peace.

205
00:17:57,118 --> 00:18:00,702
I want to see mountains again.
Mountains, Gandalf!

206
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:05,373
And then find somewhere quiet
where I can finish my book. Oh, tea.

207
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:09,543
-So you mean to go through with your plan?
-Yes, yes. It's all in hand.

208
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:11,962
All the arrangements are made.

209
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,500
Oh, thank you.

210
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,378
Frodo suspects something.

211
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:21,009
Of course he does. He's a Baggins...

212
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,849
...not some blockheaded Bracegirdle
from Hardbottle.

213
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,186
You will tell him, won't you?

214
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:30,140
-Yes, yes.
-He's very fond of you.

215
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:33,851
I know.

216
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,531
He'd probably come with me
if I asked him.

217
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,660
I think in his heart, Frodo's
still in love with the Shire.

218
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:47,573
The woods, the fields.

219
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:50,034
Little rivers.

220
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:57,212
I am old, Gandalf.

221
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:03,890
I know I don't look it, but I'm
beginning to feel it in my heart.

222
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,599
I feel thin.

223
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,395
Sort of stretched...

224
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:15,101
...like butter scraped
over too much bread.

225
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:19,781
I need a holiday. A very long holiday.

226
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:23,200
And I don't expect I shall return.

227
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:28,577
In fact, I mean not to.

228
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:35,371
Old Toby. The finest weed
in the Southfarthing.

229
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:51,721
Ah.

230
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,315
Gandalf, my old friend...

231
00:19:55,403 --> 00:19:58,270
...this will be a night to remember.

232
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,821
[CHEERING]

233
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:06,118
[MUSIC PLAYS]

234
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,126
BILBO:
Hello, hello.

235
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:26,464
Fatty Bolger. Lovely to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

236
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:30,092
Go on, Sam. Ask Rosie for a dance.

237
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:36,266
-I think I'll just have another ale.
-Oh, no, you don't.

238
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:39,105
Go on!

239
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:50,996
So there I was...

240
00:20:51,292 --> 00:20:55,376
...at the mercy
of three monstrous trolls.

241
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:57,545
And they were all arguing
amongst themselves...

242
00:20:57,631 --> 00:21:00,213
...about how they were
going to cook us.

243
00:21:00,301 --> 00:21:05,341
Whether it be turned on a spit, or to sit
on us one by one, squash us into jelly.

244
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:10,011
They spent so much time arguing
the whithertos and the whyfors...

245
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:13,686
...that the sun's first light
crept over the top of the trees...

246
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,181
...and turned them all to stone!

247
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,359
[LAUGHS]

248
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:23,855
MERRY:
Quickly.

249
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:27,908
Whoa!

250
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:30,031
Up they go!

251
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,206
No, the big one.

252
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:46,252
Mrs. Bracegirdle, how nice to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

253
00:21:46,347 --> 00:21:48,383
Are all these children yours?

254
00:21:48,474 --> 00:21:51,511
Good gracious,
you have been productive.

255
00:21:53,521 --> 00:21:54,852
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo?

256
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,226
Sackville-Bagginses!

257
00:21:58,484 --> 00:21:59,564
Quickly, hide!

258
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:11,572
Thank you, my boy.

259
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:15,494
You're a good lad, Frodo.

260
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,577
I'm very selfish, you know.

261
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:23,463
Yes, I am. Very selfish.

262
00:22:23,551 --> 00:22:25,883
I don't know why I took you in
after your mother and father died...

263
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:27,551
...but it wasn't out of charity.

264
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:29,754
I think it was because...

265
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:32,215
...of all my numerous relations...

266
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:36,010
...you were the one Baggins
that showed real spirit.

267
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:38,137
Bilbo, have you been
at the Gaffer's home brew?

268
00:22:38,232 --> 00:22:40,018
No.

269
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,983
Well, yes, but that's not the point.

270
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:46,403
The point is, Frodo...

271
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,442
...you'll be all right.

272
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,997
-Done!
-You're supposed to stick it in the ground.

273
00:22:57,084 --> 00:22:58,665
-It is in the ground.
-Outside!

274
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,288
This was your idea.

275
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:17,635
Bilbo.

276
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:21,681
Bilbo, watch out for the dragon!

277
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:25,142
Nonsense. There hasn't been a dragon
in these parts for a thousand years.

278
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:42,330
-That was good.
-Let's get another one.

279
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:48,132
GANDALF:
Meriadoc Brandybuck and Peregrin Took.

280
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:50,129
I might've known.

281
00:23:56,018 --> 00:23:58,100
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Speech, Bilbo!

282
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,389
MALE HOBBIT:
Speech!

283
00:24:00,481 --> 00:24:01,596
Speech!

284
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:09,148
My dear Bagginses and Boffins...

285
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:12,190
...Tooks and Brandybucks...

286
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:14,900
...Grubbs, Chubbs...

287
00:24:14,995 --> 00:24:16,075
...Hornblowers...

288
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,867
...Bolgers...

289
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,906
...Bracegirdles...

290
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:23,663
-...and Proudfoots.
-Proudfeet!

291
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:29,002
Today is my 111th birthday!

292
00:24:30,803 --> 00:24:32,418
Happy birthday!

293
00:24:32,513 --> 00:24:36,882
But alas, eleventy-one years is
far too short a time to live among...

294
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:39,888
...such excellent
and admirable Hobbits.

295
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:43,596
I don't know half of you
half as well as I should like...

296
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:48,355
...and I like less than half of you
half as well as you deserve.

297
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,480
I, uh--

298
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,696
I have things to do.

299
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:09,205
I've put this off far too long.

300
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:17,012
I regret to announce this is the end!

301
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,343
I'm going now.

302
00:25:20,436 --> 00:25:23,348
I bid you all a very fond farewell.

303
00:25:25,733 --> 00:25:26,939
Goodbye.

304
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,442
[HOBBITS CLAMORING]

305
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:39,280
[FOOTSTEPS]

306
00:25:50,132 --> 00:25:52,214
[LAUGHS]

307
00:26:00,184 --> 00:26:03,347
I suppose you think
that was terribly clever.

308
00:26:03,437 --> 00:26:06,929
Come on, Gandalf.
Did you see their faces?

309
00:26:07,024 --> 00:26:12,189
There are many magic rings in this world,
and none of them should be used lightly.

310
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,565
It was just a bit of fun.

311
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:18,399
Oh, you're probably right, as usual.

312
00:26:19,787 --> 00:26:23,371
-You will keep an eye on Frodo, won't you?
-Two eyes.

313
00:26:23,457 --> 00:26:26,290
As often as I can spare them.

314
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:29,664
-I'm leaving everything to him.
-What about this ring of yours?

315
00:26:29,755 --> 00:26:33,122
-Is that staying too?
-Yes, yes.

316
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:37,627
It's in an envelope over there
on the mantelpiece.

317
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:41,680
No. Wait, it's...

318
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,848
...here in my pocket.

319
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:54,727
Isn't that--? Isn't that odd, now?

320
00:26:56,365 --> 00:26:59,857
Yet, after all, why not?

321
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:06,322
-Why shouldn't I keep it?
-I think you should leave the ring behind.

322
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,991
Is that so hard?

323
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:10,451
Well, no.

324
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,376
And yes.

325
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:19,380
Now it comes to it,
I don't feel like parting with it.

326
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,424
It's mine. I found it! It came to me!

327
00:27:21,515 --> 00:27:25,804
-There's no need to get angry.
-Well, if I'm angry, it's your fault!

328
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:28,056
It's mine.

329
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,805
My own.

330
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:36,190
-My precious.
-Precious?

331
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:39,272
It's been called that before,
but not by you.

332
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:42,073
What business is it of yours
what I do with my own things?

333
00:27:42,161 --> 00:27:44,903
I think you've had that ring
quite long enough.

334
00:27:45,164 --> 00:27:48,076
-You want it for yourself!
-Bilbo Baggins!

335
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:52,410
Do not take me for some conjurer
of cheap tricks.

336
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:56,334
I am not trying to rob you.

337
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,094
I'm trying to help you.

338
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:05,969
[BILBO WHIMPERS]

339
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:14,898
All your long years,
we've been friends.

340
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:17,438
Trust me as you once did.

341
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:21,112
Let it go.

342
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:24,654
You're right, Gandalf.

343
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:29,450
The ring must go to Frodo.

344
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:33,829
It's late. The road is long.

345
00:28:33,921 --> 00:28:36,458
Yes, it is time.

346
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:41,292
-Bilbo.
-Hm?

347
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:44,294
The ring is still in your pocket.

348
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,594
Ah. Yes.

349
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:21,999
I've thought up an ending for my book:

350
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:28,719
"And he lived happily ever after
to the end of his days."

351
00:29:28,809 --> 00:29:32,301
And I'm sure you will, my dear friend.

352
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:34,811
Goodbye, Gandalf.

353
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:40,184
Goodbye, dear Bilbo.

354
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:52,204
BILBO:
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

355
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:57,117
Until our next meeting.

356
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:28,240
BILBO:
<i>It's mine. My own.</i>

357
00:30:28,327 --> 00:30:31,785
<i>My precious.</i>

358
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:35,072
Riddles in the dark.

359
00:30:35,167 --> 00:30:36,657
Bilbo!

360
00:30:36,752 --> 00:30:38,367
Bilbo!

361
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,919
My precious.

362
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:48,794
Precious.

363
00:30:48,889 --> 00:30:51,505
He's gone, hasn't he?

364
00:30:54,269 --> 00:30:57,306
He talked for so long about leaving...

365
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:00,271
...I didn't think he'd really do it.

366
00:31:04,738 --> 00:31:06,603
Gandalf?

367
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:16,576
Bilbo's ring.

368
00:31:16,917 --> 00:31:19,329
He's gone to stay with the Elves.

369
00:31:19,419 --> 00:31:22,582
He's left you Bag End.

370
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:28,792
Along with all his possessions.

371
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:31,799
The ring is yours now.

372
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,972
-Put it somewhere out of sight.
-Where are you going?

373
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:40,429
-There are some things that I must see to.
-What things?

374
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:44,813
-Questions. Questions that need answering.
-You've only just arrived.

375
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:48,311
I don't understand.

376
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:52,649
Neither do I.

377
00:31:55,956 --> 00:31:58,322
Keep it secret.

378
00:31:58,417 --> 00:32:00,203
Keep it safe.

379
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,074
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

380
00:32:35,162 --> 00:32:37,369
GOLLUM:
<i>Shire!</i>

381
00:32:37,706 --> 00:32:40,823
<i>Baggins!</i>

382
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:55,636
[THUNDER RUMBLES]

383
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:32,340
GANDALF:
<i>"The year 3434 of the Second Age.</i>

384
00:33:32,427 --> 00:33:36,966
<i>Here follows the account of Isildur,</i>
<i>High King of Gondor...</i>

385
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:40,766
<i>...and the finding</i>
<i>of the Ring of Power."</i>

386
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:46,137
<i>"It has come to me.</i>

387
00:33:46,233 --> 00:33:49,817
<i>The One Ring. It shall be</i>
<i>an heirloom of my kingdom.</i>

388
00:33:49,903 --> 00:33:53,487
<i>All those who follow in my bloodline</i>
<i>shall be bound to its fate...</i>

389
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:57,486
<i>...for I will risk</i>
<i>no hurt to the Ring.</i>

390
00:33:57,577 --> 00:34:00,114
<i>It is precious to me...</i>

391
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:03,618
<i>...though I buy it with great pain.</i>

392
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:10,962
<i>The markings upon the band</i>
<i>begin to fade.</i>

393
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:15,963
<i>The writing, which at first was as clear</i>
<i>as red flame, has all but disappeared.</i>

394
00:34:16,221 --> 00:34:20,260
<i>A secret now</i>
<i>that only fire can tell."</i>

395
00:34:24,813 --> 00:34:26,644
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

396
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:39,820
Shire.

397
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:41,947
Baggins.

398
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:46,494
There's no Bagginses around here.
They're all up in Hobbiton.

399
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,659
That way.

400
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:57,918
<i>To heal my heart and drown my woe</i>

401
00:34:58,013 --> 00:35:00,425
<i>Rain may fall and wind may blow</i>

402
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:02,551
<i>But there still be</i>

403
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:04,223
<i>Many miles to go</i>

404
00:35:04,311 --> 00:35:06,347
<i>Sweet is the sound of the pouring rain</i>

405
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,724
<i>And the stream that falls</i>
<i>From hill to plain</i>

406
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:10,726
<i>Better than rain or rippling brook</i>

407
00:35:10,817 --> 00:35:13,274
<i>Is a mug of beer inside this Took</i>

408
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:19,531
There's been some strange folk
crossing the Shire.

409
00:35:19,993 --> 00:35:23,827
Dwarves and others of a less
than savory nature.

410
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:25,696
War is brewing.

411
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:29,286
The mountains are fair teeming
with goblins.

412
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:32,084
Far-off tales and children's stories,
that's all that is.

413
00:35:32,172 --> 00:35:36,757
You're beginning to sound like that old
Bilbo Baggins. Cracked, he was.

414
00:35:36,843 --> 00:35:39,926
Young Mr. Frodo here,
he's cracking.

415
00:35:40,013 --> 00:35:41,549
And proud of it.

416
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:43,972
-Cheers, Gaffer.
-Cheers.

417
00:35:44,059 --> 00:35:48,268
It's none of our concern what goes on
beyond our borders.

418
00:35:48,355 --> 00:35:52,724
Keep your nose out of trouble,
and no trouble'll come to you.

419
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:58,312
-Good night, lads.
-Good night.

420
00:35:58,406 --> 00:36:02,991
Good night, sweet maiden
of the golden ale.

421
00:36:03,078 --> 00:36:05,569
Mind who you're sweet-talking.

422
00:36:05,664 --> 00:36:10,249
Don't worry, Sam. Rosie knows an idiot
when she sees one.

423
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:12,412
Does she?

424
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:16,080
-Good night, Sam.
-Good night, Mr. Frodo.

425
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,356
Is it secret? Is it safe?

426
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:47,865
[PIG SQUEALS]

427
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:50,580
Ah.

428
00:36:52,252 --> 00:36:54,368
What are you doing?

429
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:09,512
Hold out your hand, Frodo.

430
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:10,808
It's quite cool.

431
00:37:14,399 --> 00:37:16,139
What can you see?

432
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,318
Can you see anything?

433
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,488
Nothing.

434
00:37:25,118 --> 00:37:27,109
There's nothing.

435
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,653
Wait.

436
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:36,000
There are markings.

437
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:40,997
It's some form of Elvish.
I can't read it.

438
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:43,674
There are few who can.

439
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:49,055
The language is that of Mordor,
which I will not utter here.

440
00:37:49,684 --> 00:37:50,719
Mordor!

441
00:37:51,019 --> 00:37:53,101
In the common tongue, it says:

442
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:56,726
"One Ring to rule them all...

443
00:37:57,025 --> 00:37:59,391
...One Ring to find them...

444
00:37:59,486 --> 00:38:01,693
...One Ring to bring them all...

445
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:05,022
...and in the darkness bind them."

446
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,741
This is the One Ring...

447
00:38:08,828 --> 00:38:14,243
...forged by the Dark Lord Sauron
in the fires of Mount Doom.

448
00:38:14,334 --> 00:38:18,373
Taken by Isildur
from the hand of Sauron himself.

449
00:38:19,172 --> 00:38:21,709
Bilbo found it.

450
00:38:22,175 --> 00:38:24,086
-In Gollum's cave.
-Yes.

451
00:38:24,344 --> 00:38:28,929
For 60 years, the Ring lay quiet
in Bilbo's keeping...

452
00:38:29,015 --> 00:38:32,473
...prolonging his life,
delaying old age.

453
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:37,596
But no longer, Frodo.
Evil is stirring in Mordor.

454
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:40,102
The Ring has awoken.

455
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:43,147
It's heard its master's call.

456
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:47,197
But he was destroyed.
Sauron was destroyed.

457
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:50,570
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

458
00:38:52,914 --> 00:38:54,996
GANDALF:
No, Frodo.

459
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:59,284
The spirit of Sauron endured.

460
00:38:59,379 --> 00:39:04,749
His life force is bound to the Ring,
and the Ring survived.

461
00:39:05,093 --> 00:39:07,254
Sauron has returned.

462
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,298
His Orcs have multiplied.

463
00:39:10,390 --> 00:39:14,508
His fortress at Barad-dûr
is rebuilt in the land of Mordor.

464
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:19,517
Sauron needs only this Ring to cover
all the lands in a second darkness.

465
00:39:19,607 --> 00:39:21,814
He is seeking it.

466
00:39:21,901 --> 00:39:25,769
Seeking it. All his thought
is bent on it.

467
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:28,817
For the Ring yearns above all else...

468
00:39:28,908 --> 00:39:32,321
...to return to the hand
of its master.

469
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:34,406
They are one...

470
00:39:34,497 --> 00:39:37,660
...the Ring and the Dark Lord.

471
00:39:37,750 --> 00:39:38,830
Frodo...

472
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:41,330
...he must never find it.

473
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:42,536
FRODO:
All right.

474
00:39:42,839 --> 00:39:47,208
We put it away. We keep it hidden.
We never speak of it again.

475
00:39:47,302 --> 00:39:50,044
No one knows it's here, do they?

476
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:56,925
Do they, Gandalf?

477
00:39:57,979 --> 00:40:01,346
There is one other who knew
that Bilbo had the Ring.

478
00:40:02,650 --> 00:40:05,687
I looked everywhere
for the creature Gollum.

479
00:40:05,778 --> 00:40:08,064
But the enemy found him first.

480
00:40:08,156 --> 00:40:09,566
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

481
00:40:09,657 --> 00:40:12,239
GANDALF: <i>I don't know how long</i>
<i>they tortured him.</i>

482
00:40:12,327 --> 00:40:16,946
<i>But amidst the endless screams and</i>
<i>inane babble, they discerned two words:</i>

483
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:19,247
GOLLUM:
Shire!

484
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,074
Baggins!

485
00:40:21,169 --> 00:40:23,080
Shire.

486
00:40:23,171 --> 00:40:26,163
Baggins. But that would
lead them here!

487
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:30,003
Who goes there?

488
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:32,961
Take it, Gandalf!

489
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:34,463
-Take it!
-No, Frodo.

490
00:40:34,557 --> 00:40:37,048
-You must take it!
-You cannot offer me this ring!

491
00:40:37,143 --> 00:40:40,510
-I'm giving it to you!
-Don't tempt me, Frodo!

492
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:44,230
I dare not take it.

493
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:47,021
Not even to keep it safe.

494
00:40:48,196 --> 00:40:50,187
Understand, Frodo...

495
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:54,483
...I would use this Ring
from a desire to do good.

496
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:05,619
But through me, it would wield a power
too great and terrible to imagine.

497
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:09,126
-But it cannot stay in the Shire!
-No.

498
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,625
No, it can't.

499
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,344
What must I do?

500
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:24,604
-You must leave. And leave quickly.
-Where? Where do I go?

501
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:28,024
Get out of the Shire.
Make for the village of Bree.

502
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,437
Bree.

503
00:41:29,529 --> 00:41:32,441
-What about you?
-I'll be waiting for you...

504
00:41:32,532 --> 00:41:35,114
...at the inn of the Prancing Pony.

505
00:41:35,201 --> 00:41:39,035
-And the Ring will be safe there?
-I don't know, Frodo.

506
00:41:39,122 --> 00:41:41,158
I don't have any answers.

507
00:41:42,667 --> 00:41:48,287
I must see the head of my order. He is
both wise and powerful. Trust me, Frodo.

508
00:41:48,381 --> 00:41:50,542
He'll know what to do.

509
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:53,962
You'll have to leave the name
of Baggins behind you.

510
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:56,753
That name is not safe
outside the Shire.

511
00:41:57,390 --> 00:42:00,678
Travel only by day.
And stay off the road.

512
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,473
I can cut across country
easily enough.

513
00:42:06,983 --> 00:42:08,314
My dear Frodo.

514
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:11,692
Hobbits really are amazing creatures.

515
00:42:11,779 --> 00:42:14,816
You can learn all that there is to
know about their ways in a month.

516
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:17,364
And yet, after a hundred years...

517
00:42:17,452 --> 00:42:19,659
...they can still surprise you.

518
00:42:19,746 --> 00:42:20,952
[RUSTLING]

519
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:22,490
Get down.

520
00:42:31,132 --> 00:42:32,247
[GROANING]

521
00:42:34,802 --> 00:42:38,294
Confound it all, Samwise Gamgee!
Have you been eavesdropping?

522
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:42,974
I haven't been dropping no eaves. Honest.
I was cutting the grass under the window.

523
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:45,598
A little late for trimming the verge,
don't you think?

524
00:42:45,688 --> 00:42:48,680
-I heard raised voices.
-What did you hear? Speak!

525
00:42:48,775 --> 00:42:49,855
Nothing important.

526
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:54,607
That is, I heard a good deal about a ring,
a Dark Lord and the end of the world but--

527
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:59,487
Please, Mr. Gandalf, sir, don't hurt me.
Don't turn me into anything unnatural.

528
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:01,822
No?

529
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:04,157
Perhaps not.

530
00:43:05,374 --> 00:43:08,832
I've thought of a better use for you.

531
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:13,538
GANDALF:
Come along, Samwise. Keep up.

532
00:43:15,051 --> 00:43:17,417
Be careful, both of you.

533
00:43:17,512 --> 00:43:20,424
The enemy has many spies
in his service:

534
00:43:20,515 --> 00:43:23,507
Birds, beasts.

535
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,055
Is it safe?

536
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,229
Never put it on...

537
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:33,774
...for the agents of the Dark Lord
will be drawn to its power.

538
00:43:33,861 --> 00:43:35,397
Always remember, Frodo...

539
00:43:35,905 --> 00:43:39,068
...the Ring is trying to get back
to its master.

540
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:41,574
It wants to be found.

541
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:51,785
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

542
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:24,408
This is it.

543
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,906
This is what?

544
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:29,242
If I take one more step...

545
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:33,618
...it'll be the farthest away
from home I've ever been.

546
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:39,415
Come on, Sam.

547
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:49,638
Remember what Bilbo used to say:

548
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:54,017
-"It's a dangerous business, Frodo."
BILBO: <i>"Going out your door.</i>

549
00:44:54,108 --> 00:44:58,647
<i>You step onto the road,</i>
<i>and if you don't keep your feet...</i>

550
00:44:58,738 --> 00:45:02,947
<i>...there's no knowing where</i>
<i>you might be swept off to."</i>

551
00:45:11,584 --> 00:45:13,950
[SINGING]

552
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:18,795
Sam.

553
00:45:22,303 --> 00:45:23,418
Wood-elves.

554
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:40,643
They're going to the harbor
beyond the White Towers.

555
00:45:41,197 --> 00:45:42,983
To the Grey Havens.

556
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,656
SAM:
They're leaving Middle-earth.

557
00:45:45,743 --> 00:45:47,984
FRODO:
Never to return.

558
00:45:50,873 --> 00:45:52,989
I don't know why...

559
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:56,080
...it makes me sad.

560
00:45:58,172 --> 00:46:02,791
Everywhere I lie there's a dirty
great root sticking into my back.

561
00:46:03,511 --> 00:46:05,251
Just shut your eyes...

562
00:46:05,346 --> 00:46:08,213
...and imagine you're back
in your own bed...

563
00:46:08,307 --> 00:46:12,300
...with a soft mattress
and a lovely feather pillow.

564
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:24,354
It's not working, Mr. Frodo.

565
00:46:24,448 --> 00:46:27,360
I'm never going to be able
to sleep out here.

566
00:46:29,704 --> 00:46:32,036
Me neither, Sam.

567
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:03,651
MALE VOICE: <i>Smoke rises</i>
<i>from the Mountain of Doom.</i>

568
00:47:03,738 --> 00:47:05,524
<i>The hour grows late.</i>

569
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:09,277
<i>And Gandalf the Grey</i>
<i>rides to Isengard...</i>

570
00:47:09,368 --> 00:47:11,950
<i>...seeking my counsel.</i>

571
00:47:12,038 --> 00:47:16,122
For that is why you have come,
is it not?

572
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:17,539
My old friend.

573
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:19,408
Saruman.

574
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:27,253
SARUMAN: You are sure of this?
GANDALF: Beyond any doubt.

575
00:47:28,054 --> 00:47:30,340
So the Ring of Power has been found.

576
00:47:30,431 --> 00:47:33,764
All these long years,
it was in the Shire.

577
00:47:33,851 --> 00:47:37,059
-Under my very nose.
-Yet you did not have the wit to see it.

578
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:42,182
Your love of the halfling's leaf
has clearly slowed your mind.

579
00:47:43,069 --> 00:47:47,108
But we still have time. Time enough
to counter Sauron if we act quickly.

580
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:48,688
Time?

581
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:52,233
What time do you think we have?

582
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:56,616
Sauron has regained
much of his former strength.

583
00:47:56,707 --> 00:47:58,948
He cannot yet take physical form...

584
00:47:59,210 --> 00:48:01,917
...but his spirit has lost
none of its potency.

585
00:48:02,588 --> 00:48:07,628
Concealed within his fortress,
the Lord of Mordor sees all.

586
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:14,135
His gaze pierces cloud, shadow,
earth and flesh.

587
00:48:15,643 --> 00:48:18,806
You know of what I speak, Gandalf.

588
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:24,975
A Great Eye, lidless,
wreathed in flame.

589
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:27,810
The Eye of Sauron.

590
00:48:27,905 --> 00:48:30,612
He is gathering all evil to him.

591
00:48:30,699 --> 00:48:33,281
Very soon, he'll have summoned
an army great enough...

592
00:48:33,369 --> 00:48:35,610
...for an assault upon Middle-earth.

593
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:38,321
You know this?

594
00:48:38,833 --> 00:48:40,323
How?

595
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,621
I have seen it.

596
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:46,253
A palantír is a dangerous tool,
Saruman.

597
00:48:46,966 --> 00:48:48,456
Why?

598
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:51,633
Why should we fear to use it?

599
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:58,224
They are not all accounted for,
the lost Seeing-stones.

600
00:48:58,310 --> 00:49:01,598
We do not know who else
may be watching.

601
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:06,978
The hour is later than you think.

602
00:49:07,069 --> 00:49:09,435
Sauron's forces are already moving.

603
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:14,441
The Nine have left Minas Morgul.

604
00:49:14,827 --> 00:49:15,907
The Nine?

605
00:49:15,995 --> 00:49:19,158
They crossed the River Isen
on Midsummer's Eve...

606
00:49:19,248 --> 00:49:22,035
...disguised as riders in black.

607
00:49:22,126 --> 00:49:26,119
-They've reached the Shire?
-They will find the Ring.

608
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:29,956
And kill the one who carries it.

609
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:31,958
Frodo!

610
00:49:44,565 --> 00:49:48,979
You did not seriously think that a Hobbit
could contend with the will of Sauron?

611
00:49:49,737 --> 00:49:52,524
There are none who can.

612
00:49:55,034 --> 00:49:57,776
Against the power of Mordor...

613
00:49:57,870 --> 00:50:00,577
...there can be no victory.

614
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:05,704
We must join with him, Gandalf.

615
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:09,336
We must join with Sauron.

616
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:14,671
It would be wise, my friend.

617
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:16,627
Tell me...

618
00:50:16,722 --> 00:50:17,837
...friend...

619
00:50:18,849 --> 00:50:23,388
...when did Saruman the Wise
abandon reason for madness?

620
00:51:02,893 --> 00:51:04,599
I gave you the chance...

621
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:08,436
...of aiding me willingly...

622
00:51:08,524 --> 00:51:12,733
...but you have elected
the way of pain!

623
00:51:36,010 --> 00:51:37,500
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

624
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:39,923
Frodo? Frodo!

625
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:44,636
-I thought I'd lost you.
-What are you talking about?

626
00:51:44,727 --> 00:51:47,764
-It's just something Gandalf said.
-What did he say?

627
00:51:48,606 --> 00:51:52,474
"Don't you lose him, Samwise Gamgee."
And I don't mean to.

628
00:51:52,735 --> 00:51:56,353
Sam, we're still in the Shire.
What could possibly happen?

629
00:51:59,325 --> 00:52:00,360
Frodo.

630
00:52:00,618 --> 00:52:02,904
-Merry, it's Frodo Baggins.
-Hello, Frodo.

631
00:52:02,995 --> 00:52:04,451
Get off him.

632
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:06,491
Come on, Frodo.

633
00:52:06,582 --> 00:52:08,493
FRODO:
What's the meaning of this?

634
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:10,699
You've been into Farmer Maggot's crop!

635
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:12,121
[DOG BARKS]

636
00:52:13,213 --> 00:52:15,329
MAGGOT:
You get back here!

637
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:17,707
Get out of my field!

638
00:52:17,801 --> 00:52:20,759
You'll know the devil
if I catch up with you!

639
00:52:20,846 --> 00:52:23,883
MERRY: I don't know why he's so upset.
It's only a couple of carrots.

640
00:52:23,974 --> 00:52:25,180
PIPPIN:
And some cabbages.

641
00:52:25,267 --> 00:52:28,259
And those three bags of potatoes
that we lifted last week.

642
00:52:28,354 --> 00:52:32,563
-And then the mushrooms the week before.
MERRY: Yes, Pippin. My point is...

643
00:52:32,650 --> 00:52:34,936
...he's clearly overreacting.

644
00:52:35,027 --> 00:52:36,563
Run!

645
00:52:50,042 --> 00:52:52,579
Oh, that was close.

646
00:52:53,671 --> 00:52:56,788
I think I've broken something.

647
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:00,212
Trust a Brandybuck and a Took!

648
00:53:00,302 --> 00:53:04,045
What? That was just a detour.
A short cut.

649
00:53:04,139 --> 00:53:06,425
-Short cut to what?
-Mushrooms!

650
00:53:15,192 --> 00:53:16,682
PIPPIN:
That's mine.

651
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,061
That's nice, Merry.

652
00:53:21,615 --> 00:53:23,697
MERRY:
Here's a nice one, Sam.

653
00:53:23,784 --> 00:53:26,366
I think we should get off the road.

654
00:53:27,955 --> 00:53:31,618
[SCREECHING]

655
00:53:35,546 --> 00:53:37,002
Get off the road!

656
00:53:37,089 --> 00:53:38,625
Quick!

657
00:53:46,974 --> 00:53:51,058
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

658
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:52,801
Be quiet!

659
00:54:19,923 --> 00:54:21,663
[SNIFFS]

660
00:54:59,129 --> 00:55:01,290
What was that?

661
00:55:20,567 --> 00:55:22,683
[SCREECHES]

662
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:35,487
SAM:
Anything?

663
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,656
Nothing.

664
00:55:38,377 --> 00:55:40,663
What is going on?

665
00:55:41,213 --> 00:55:45,001
That Black Rider was looking
for something. Or someone.

666
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,833
Frodo?

667
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:49,589
Get down!

668
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:08,771
I have to leave the Shire.

669
00:56:09,783 --> 00:56:12,149
Sam and I must get to Bree.

670
00:56:12,244 --> 00:56:13,700
Right.

671
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:17,366
Bucklebury Ferry. Follow me.

672
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:26,997
PIPPIN:
Run!

673
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,209
MERRY:
This way! Follow me!

674
00:56:33,765 --> 00:56:34,800
PIPPIN:
Run!

675
00:56:48,071 --> 00:56:49,811
MERRY:
Get the rope, Sam!

676
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:54,028
Frodo!

677
00:56:54,745 --> 00:56:56,155
PIPPIN:
Run, Frodo!

678
00:56:56,496 --> 00:56:57,656
FRODO: Go!
PIPPIN: Hurry!

679
00:56:57,748 --> 00:57:00,410
MERRY:
Frodo, come on!

680
00:57:01,335 --> 00:57:03,326
SAM: Come on! Faster!
PIPPIN: Jump!

681
00:57:10,302 --> 00:57:11,792
[SCREECHES]

682
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:22,519
-How far to the nearest crossing?
-The Brandywine Bridge. 20 miles.

683
00:57:37,120 --> 00:57:38,610
Come on.

684
00:57:49,800 --> 00:57:53,213
-What do you want?
-We're heading for the Prancing Pony.

685
00:57:56,723 --> 00:57:59,590
Hobbits. Four Hobbits!

686
00:57:59,685 --> 00:58:03,678
What's more, out of the Shire by your
talk. What business brings you to Bree?

687
00:58:04,106 --> 00:58:07,223
We wish to stay at the inn.
Our business is our own.

688
00:58:08,235 --> 00:58:10,851
All right, young sir.
I meant no offense.

689
00:58:10,946 --> 00:58:13,562
It's my job to ask questions
after nightfall.

690
00:58:13,657 --> 00:58:16,569
There's talk of strange folk abroad.

691
00:58:16,660 --> 00:58:18,867
Can't be too careful.

692
00:58:38,598 --> 00:58:42,090
Out of the way!
Watch where you're walking.

693
00:58:49,443 --> 00:58:52,150
[LAUGHING]

694
00:59:06,251 --> 00:59:07,866
Excuse me.

695
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:11,746
Good evening, little masters.
What can I do for you?

696
00:59:11,840 --> 00:59:18,052
If you're seeking accommodation, we got
some cozy Hobbit-sized rooms available.

697
00:59:18,138 --> 00:59:22,802
Always proud to cater
to the Little Folk, Mister...?

698
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,013
Underhill. My name's Underhill.

699
00:59:27,314 --> 00:59:29,851
-Underhill, yes.
-We're friends of Gandalf the Grey.

700
00:59:29,941 --> 00:59:33,149
-Can you tell him we've arrived?
-Gandalf?

701
00:59:33,570 --> 00:59:35,310
Gandalf.

702
00:59:36,156 --> 00:59:37,896
Oh, yes...

703
00:59:37,991 --> 00:59:40,152
...I remember. Elderly chap.

704
00:59:40,494 --> 00:59:43,406
Big grey beard, pointy hat.

705
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:45,661
Not seen him for six months.

706
00:59:52,422 --> 00:59:53,707
What do we do now?

707
01:00:00,931 --> 01:00:02,216
Sam...

708
01:00:02,307 --> 01:00:04,218
...he'll be here. He'll come.

709
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:09,056
MAN:
Get out of my way!

710
01:00:11,441 --> 01:00:13,102
What's that?

711
01:00:13,360 --> 01:00:15,897
This, my friend, is a pint.

712
01:00:15,987 --> 01:00:17,693
It comes in pints?

713
01:00:18,031 --> 01:00:21,740
-I'm getting one.
-You got a whole half already!

714
01:00:28,083 --> 01:00:31,917
That fellow's done nothing
but stare at you since we arrived.

715
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:36,955
Excuse me.

716
01:00:38,760 --> 01:00:41,752
That Man in the corner. Who is he?

717
01:00:42,931 --> 01:00:47,345
He's one of them Rangers. They're
dangerous folk, wandering the Wilds.

718
01:00:47,602 --> 01:00:52,096
What his right name is, I've never heard,
but around here he's known as Strider.

719
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,724
Strider.

720
01:01:08,748 --> 01:01:11,956
VOICE OF THE RING:
<i>Baggins.</i>

721
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:16,957
<i>Baggins.</i>

722
01:01:22,345 --> 01:01:27,465
<i>Baggins. Baggins.</i>

723
01:01:29,311 --> 01:01:31,597
PIPPIN:
Baggins? Sure, I know a Baggins.

724
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:35,309
He's over there. Frodo Baggins.

725
01:01:35,400 --> 01:01:38,517
He's my second cousin,
once removed on his mother's side...

726
01:01:38,612 --> 01:01:40,944
...and my third cousin, twice removed....

727
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:47,192
-Pippin!
-Steady on, Frodo.

728
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:19,190
SAURON:
You cannot hide.

729
01:02:22,155 --> 01:02:25,318
I see you.

730
01:02:26,993 --> 01:02:29,735
There is no life...

731
01:02:29,829 --> 01:02:32,115
...in the void.

732
01:02:32,207 --> 01:02:33,743
Only...

733
01:02:34,668 --> 01:02:36,158
...death.

734
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:47,044
You draw far too much attention
to yourself, "Mr. Underhill."

735
01:02:51,726 --> 01:02:52,841
What do you want?

736
01:02:52,936 --> 01:02:55,018
A little more caution from you.
That is no trinket you carry.

737
01:02:55,397 --> 01:02:58,389
-I carry nothing.
-Indeed.

738
01:02:58,692 --> 01:03:01,274
I can avoid being seen if I wish...

739
01:03:01,361 --> 01:03:05,104
...but to disappear entirely,
that is a rare gift.

740
01:03:05,615 --> 01:03:08,231
-Who are you?
-Are you frightened?

741
01:03:09,494 --> 01:03:10,574
Yes.

742
01:03:10,662 --> 01:03:14,621
Not nearly frightened enough.
I know what hunts you.

743
01:03:16,418 --> 01:03:17,874
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

744
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:21,165
Let him go!
Or I'll have you, Longshanks.

745
01:03:22,841 --> 01:03:27,005
You have a stout heart, little Hobbit.
But that will not save you.

746
01:03:27,095 --> 01:03:30,087
You can no longer wait
for the wizard, Frodo.

747
01:03:30,181 --> 01:03:31,216
They're coming.

748
01:03:31,683 --> 01:03:34,516
[HORSE GRUNTS]

749
01:04:41,378 --> 01:04:43,619
[SCREECHING]

750
01:04:54,933 --> 01:04:56,423
What are they?

751
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:00,719
They were once Men.

752
01:05:01,231 --> 01:05:03,517
Great kings of Men.

753
01:05:03,608 --> 01:05:06,816
Then Sauron the Deceiver gave to them
nine rings of power.

754
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:10,487
Blinded by their greed,
they took them without question.

755
01:05:10,740 --> 01:05:14,107
One by one, falling into darkness.

756
01:05:14,202 --> 01:05:16,739
Now they are slaves to his will.

757
01:05:19,124 --> 01:05:20,864
They are the Nazgûl.

758
01:05:20,959 --> 01:05:23,746
Ringwraiths. Neither living nor dead.

759
01:05:24,504 --> 01:05:25,994
At all times they feel...

760
01:05:26,089 --> 01:05:28,125
<i>...the presence of the Ring...</i>

761
01:05:28,216 --> 01:05:32,801
<i>...drawn to the power of the One.</i>
<i>They will never stop hunting you.</i>

762
01:05:42,772 --> 01:05:45,684
FRODO: Where are you taking us?
-Into the Wild.

763
01:05:53,867 --> 01:05:58,031
How do we know this Strider
is a friend of Gandalf?

764
01:05:58,121 --> 01:06:00,988
I think a servant of the enemy
would look fairer...

765
01:06:01,374 --> 01:06:05,287
-...and feel fouler.
-He's foul enough.

766
01:06:05,879 --> 01:06:08,746
We have no choice but to trust him.

767
01:06:08,840 --> 01:06:12,332
-But where is he leading us?
STRIDER: To Rivendell, Master Gamgee.

768
01:06:14,721 --> 01:06:18,009
-To the house of Elrond.
SAM: Did you hear that? Rivendell.

769
01:06:18,558 --> 01:06:21,345
We're going to see the Elves.

770
01:06:38,620 --> 01:06:40,235
[HOBBITS WHISPERING]

771
01:06:42,999 --> 01:06:47,288
-Gentlemen, we do not stop till nightfall.
-What about breakfast?

772
01:06:47,378 --> 01:06:50,120
-You've already had it.
-We've had one, yes.

773
01:06:50,215 --> 01:06:52,501
What about second breakfast?

774
01:06:55,929 --> 01:06:59,137
Don't think he knows
about second breakfast, Pip.

775
01:06:59,224 --> 01:07:04,594
What about elevenses? Luncheon?
Afternoon tea? Dinner? Supper?

776
01:07:04,687 --> 01:07:08,896
-He knows about them, doesn't he?
-I wouldn't count on it.

777
01:07:14,364 --> 01:07:15,945
MERRY:
Pippin!

778
01:07:32,465 --> 01:07:35,957
What do they eat
when they can't get Hobbit?

779
01:07:56,406 --> 01:07:59,318
[STRIDER HUMS]

780
01:08:03,788 --> 01:08:07,406
[STRIDER SINGS IN ELVISH]

781
01:08:14,632 --> 01:08:16,839
Who is she?

782
01:08:17,510 --> 01:08:20,126
This woman you sing of.

783
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:26,007
'Tis the lady of Lúthien.

784
01:08:26,102 --> 01:08:31,313
The Elf-maiden who gave her love
to Beren, a mortal.

785
01:08:33,151 --> 01:08:35,267
What happened to her?

786
01:08:37,488 --> 01:08:39,979
She died.

787
01:08:44,037 --> 01:08:46,369
Get some sleep, Frodo.

788
01:08:56,633 --> 01:09:00,751
SARUMAN: <i>The power of Isengard</i>
<i>is at your command...</i>

789
01:09:00,845 --> 01:09:05,339
<i>...Sauron, Lord of the Earth.</i>

790
01:09:06,017 --> 01:09:08,349
[VOICES WHISPERING IN BLACK SPEECH]

791
01:09:08,686 --> 01:09:14,477
SAURON:
<i>Build me an army worthy of Mordor.</i>

792
01:09:20,198 --> 01:09:24,658
What orders from Mordor, my lord?
What does the Eye command?

793
01:09:25,078 --> 01:09:27,034
We have work to do.

794
01:10:09,622 --> 01:10:14,241
The trees are strong, my lord.
Their roots go deep.

795
01:10:14,627 --> 01:10:16,458
Rip them all down.

796
01:10:43,906 --> 01:10:46,773
This was the great watchtower
of Amon Sûl.

797
01:10:48,494 --> 01:10:51,156
We shall rest here tonight.

798
01:11:02,884 --> 01:11:06,376
These are for you.
Keep them close.

799
01:11:06,471 --> 01:11:09,008
I'm going to have a look around.

800
01:11:11,392 --> 01:11:13,303
Stay here.

801
01:11:15,855 --> 01:11:18,016
MERRY:
My tomato's burst.

802
01:11:18,274 --> 01:11:20,230
PIPPIN:
Could I have some bacon?

803
01:11:20,318 --> 01:11:22,309
MERRY:
Want a tomato, Sam?

804
01:11:22,695 --> 01:11:26,404
-What are you doing?!
-Tomatoes, sausages, nice crispy bacon.

805
01:11:26,491 --> 01:11:29,358
SAM: We saved some for you, Mr. Frodo.
FRODO: Put it out, you fools!

806
01:11:29,452 --> 01:11:33,491
-Put it out!
PIPPIN: That's nice! Ash on my tomatoes!

807
01:11:34,040 --> 01:11:36,156
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

808
01:11:41,923 --> 01:11:43,663
Go!

809
01:12:37,103 --> 01:12:38,559
Back, you devils!

810
01:12:49,031 --> 01:12:51,613
[VOICE OF THE RING
SPEAKS IN BLACK SPEECH]

811
01:13:30,823 --> 01:13:33,781
[VOICE OF THE RING
SPEAKS IN BLACK SPEECH]

812
01:14:02,063 --> 01:14:03,303
Frodo!

813
01:14:07,360 --> 01:14:09,191
-Frodo.
-Oh, Sam.

814
01:14:46,232 --> 01:14:47,221
Strider!

815
01:14:50,027 --> 01:14:55,522
-Help him, Strider.
-He's been stabbed by a Morgul blade.

816
01:14:57,034 --> 01:15:01,903
This is beyond my skill to heal.
He needs Elvish medicine.

817
01:15:06,502 --> 01:15:07,617
Hurry!

818
01:15:07,712 --> 01:15:11,796
We're six days from Rivendell!
He'll never make it!

819
01:15:11,882 --> 01:15:13,747
Hold on, Frodo.

820
01:15:15,553 --> 01:15:16,588
Gandalf!

821
01:15:33,279 --> 01:15:36,396
[METAL CLANKING]

822
01:16:14,111 --> 01:16:17,319
[WHISPERS INSTRUCTIONS TO THE MOTH]

823
01:17:09,750 --> 01:17:11,035
[GROWLS]

824
01:17:54,295 --> 01:17:57,378
Look, Frodo. It's Mr. Bilbo's trolls.

825
01:17:59,550 --> 01:18:02,383
Mr. Frodo? He's going cold.

826
01:18:05,347 --> 01:18:07,178
Is he going to die?

827
01:18:07,266 --> 01:18:12,181
He's passing into the Shadow World.
He'll soon become a Wraith like them.

828
01:18:12,438 --> 01:18:14,019
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

829
01:18:17,359 --> 01:18:21,227
-They're close.
-Sam, do you know the Athelas plant?

830
01:18:21,322 --> 01:18:22,903
-Athelas?
-Kingsfoil.

831
01:18:22,990 --> 01:18:24,196
Kingsfoil, aye, it's a weed.

832
01:18:24,283 --> 01:18:27,446
It may help to slow the poisoning.
Hurry!

833
01:18:41,842 --> 01:18:45,960
FEMALE: What's this?
A Ranger caught off his guard?

834
01:19:10,871 --> 01:19:11,906
Frodo.

835
01:19:13,874 --> 01:19:16,991
[IN ELVISH]

836
01:19:28,847 --> 01:19:30,678
Who is she?

837
01:19:31,350 --> 01:19:33,090
[IN ENGLISH]
Frodo.

838
01:19:33,352 --> 01:19:36,844
-She's an Elf.
-He's fading.

839
01:19:39,108 --> 01:19:41,349
He's not going to last.

840
01:19:41,443 --> 01:19:44,150
We must get him to my father.

841
01:19:44,905 --> 01:19:47,817
-I've been looking for you for two days.
-Where are you taking him?

842
01:19:47,908 --> 01:19:54,029
There are five Wraiths behind you.
Where the other four are, I do not know.

843
01:19:55,124 --> 01:19:57,581
[IN ELVISH]

844
01:19:57,668 --> 01:19:59,374
[IN ELVISH]

845
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:03,211
What are they saying?

846
01:20:03,299 --> 01:20:05,335
ARWEN:

847
01:20:09,221 --> 01:20:10,882
[IN ENGLISH]
I do not fear them.

848
01:20:14,685 --> 01:20:16,641
[SPEAKS ELVISH]

849
01:20:20,733 --> 01:20:22,189
[IN ENGLISH]
Arwen...

850
01:20:22,276 --> 01:20:25,518
...ride hard. Don't look back.

851
01:20:30,576 --> 01:20:34,945
What are you doing?!
Those Wraiths are still out there!

852
01:21:41,814 --> 01:21:42,974
[SCREECHES]

853
01:21:45,109 --> 01:21:47,646
[SPEAKS ELVISH]

854
01:22:29,570 --> 01:22:32,277
Give up the halfling, She-Elf.

855
01:22:33,198 --> 01:22:35,780
If you want him, come and claim him.

856
01:22:47,838 --> 01:22:50,045
[SPEAKS ELVISH]

857
01:23:29,671 --> 01:23:32,162
No. No!

858
01:23:35,427 --> 01:23:37,793
Frodo, no.

859
01:23:37,888 --> 01:23:40,300
Frodo, don't give in.

860
01:23:40,390 --> 01:23:42,426
Not now.

861
01:23:53,362 --> 01:23:55,853
ARWEN:
<i>What grace is given me...</i>

862
01:23:56,532 --> 01:23:58,363
<i>...let it pass to him.</i>

863
01:23:58,617 --> 01:24:00,733
<i>Let him be spared.</i>

864
01:24:01,370 --> 01:24:03,406
<i>Save him.</i>

865
01:24:05,374 --> 01:24:08,787
[SPEAKS ELVISH]

866
01:24:15,801 --> 01:24:20,966
-Where am I?
GANDALF: You are in the house of Elrond.

867
01:24:21,431 --> 01:24:27,927
And it is 10:00 in the morning
on October 24th, if you want to know.

868
01:24:29,898 --> 01:24:33,686
-Gandalf!
-Yes, I'm here.

869
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:38,403
And you're lucky to be here too.

870
01:24:39,074 --> 01:24:43,158
A few more hours and you
would have been beyond our aid.

871
01:24:43,245 --> 01:24:47,409
But you have some strength in you,
my dear Hobbit.

872
01:24:55,007 --> 01:24:57,498
What happened, Gandalf?

873
01:24:58,468 --> 01:25:03,838
-Why didn't you meet us?
-I am sorry, Frodo.

874
01:25:08,604 --> 01:25:10,344
I was delayed.

875
01:25:11,231 --> 01:25:15,440
A friendship with Saruman
is not lightly thrown aside.

876
01:25:19,531 --> 01:25:24,195
One ill turn deserves another.
It is over.

877
01:25:24,494 --> 01:25:27,236
Embrace the power of the Ring...

878
01:25:27,789 --> 01:25:30,326
...or embrace your own destruction!

879
01:25:32,628 --> 01:25:36,496
GANDALF:
There is only one Lord of the Ring.

880
01:25:36,757 --> 01:25:40,750
Only one who can bend it to his will.

881
01:25:41,553 --> 01:25:45,512
And he does not share power.

882
01:25:45,766 --> 01:25:48,508
[BIRD SCREECHES]

883
01:25:59,863 --> 01:26:03,230
So you have chosen death.

884
01:26:13,293 --> 01:26:17,081
Gandalf? What is it?

885
01:26:18,048 --> 01:26:19,834
Nothing, Frodo.

886
01:26:20,509 --> 01:26:22,420
SAM:
Frodo!

887
01:26:22,511 --> 01:26:23,671
Frodo!

888
01:26:23,762 --> 01:26:26,253
-Sam.
-Bless you, you're awake!

889
01:26:26,348 --> 01:26:29,090
Sam has hardly left your side.

890
01:26:29,351 --> 01:26:31,512
We were that worried about you.
Weren't we, Mr. Gandalf?

891
01:26:31,895 --> 01:26:37,015
By the skills of Lord Elrond,
you're beginning to mend.

892
01:26:38,527 --> 01:26:42,111
Welcome to Rivendell, Frodo Baggins.

893
01:27:30,162 --> 01:27:33,529
FRODO: Bilbo!
-Hello, Frodo, my lad.

894
01:27:33,623 --> 01:27:35,363
Bilbo.

895
01:27:40,380 --> 01:27:42,120
FRODO:
<i>"There and Back Again:</i>

896
01:27:42,382 --> 01:27:45,124
<i>A Hobbit's Tale</i>, by Bilbo Baggins."

897
01:27:48,180 --> 01:27:51,764
-This is wonderful.
-I meant to go back...

898
01:27:52,100 --> 01:27:55,888
...wonder at the powers of Mirkwood...

899
01:27:56,354 --> 01:27:58,640
...visit Lake-town...

900
01:27:58,899 --> 01:28:02,266
...see the Lonely Mountain again.

901
01:28:02,694 --> 01:28:07,609
But age, it seems,
has finally caught up with me.

902
01:28:19,711 --> 01:28:21,497
FRODO:
I miss the Shire.

903
01:28:21,922 --> 01:28:27,042
I spent all my childhood pretending
I was off somewhere else.

904
01:28:27,385 --> 01:28:30,969
Off with you,
on one of your adventures.

905
01:28:33,934 --> 01:28:37,518
But my own adventure turned out
to be quite different.

906
01:28:42,734 --> 01:28:45,942
I'm not like you, Bilbo.

907
01:28:47,072 --> 01:28:49,404
My dear boy.

908
01:28:53,495 --> 01:28:57,454
SAM: Now, what have I forgotten?
-Packed already?

909
01:28:58,250 --> 01:29:00,115
No harm in being prepared.

910
01:29:00,210 --> 01:29:02,872
-I thought you wanted to see the Elves.
-I do.

911
01:29:02,963 --> 01:29:05,955
-More than anything.
-I did.

912
01:29:06,049 --> 01:29:08,005
It's just....

913
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:11,467
We did what Gandalf wanted, didn't we?

914
01:29:11,555 --> 01:29:15,343
We got the Ring this far,
to Rivendell. And I thought...

915
01:29:15,433 --> 01:29:18,846
...seeing as how you're on the mend,
we'd be off soon.

916
01:29:18,937 --> 01:29:20,677
Off home.

917
01:29:24,860 --> 01:29:26,851
You are right, Sam.

918
01:29:29,030 --> 01:29:31,772
We did what we set out to do.

919
01:29:32,367 --> 01:29:34,949
The Ring will be safe in Rivendell.

920
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:41,372
I am ready to go home.

921
01:29:42,127 --> 01:29:44,243
ELROND:
His strength returns.

922
01:29:44,337 --> 01:29:50,082
That wound will never fully heal.
He will carry it the rest of his life.

923
01:29:50,635 --> 01:29:53,251
And yet to have come so far
still bearing the Ring...

924
01:29:53,346 --> 01:29:57,180
...the Hobbit has shown extraordinary
resilience to its evil.

925
01:29:57,267 --> 01:30:00,634
It is a burden he should never
have had to bear.

926
01:30:00,896 --> 01:30:06,391
-We can ask no more of Frodo.
-Gandalf, the enemy is moving.

927
01:30:06,484 --> 01:30:11,148
Sauron's forces are massing in the East.
His Eye is fixed on Rivendell.

928
01:30:11,406 --> 01:30:14,193
And Saruman, you tell me, has betrayed us.

929
01:30:14,284 --> 01:30:17,572
Our list of allies grows thin.

930
01:30:18,330 --> 01:30:21,197
His treachery runs deeper
than you know.

931
01:30:21,291 --> 01:30:25,034
By foul craft, Saruman
has crossed Orcs with Goblin-men.

932
01:30:25,128 --> 01:30:27,619
He's breeding an army
in the caverns of Isengard.

933
01:30:27,923 --> 01:30:32,542
An army that can move in sunlight
and cover great distance at speed.

934
01:30:32,636 --> 01:30:35,093
Saruman is coming for the Ring.

935
01:30:35,555 --> 01:30:39,673
This evil cannot be concealed
by the power of the Elves.

936
01:30:39,768 --> 01:30:44,182
We do not have the strength
to fight both Mordor and Isengard!

937
01:30:48,026 --> 01:30:49,106
Gandalf...

938
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:53,027
...the Ring cannot stay here.

939
01:31:12,550 --> 01:31:15,713
ELROND: <i>This peril belongs</i>
<i>to all Middle-earth.</i>

940
01:31:15,971 --> 01:31:18,678
<i>They must decide now how to end it.</i>

941
01:31:19,724 --> 01:31:23,308
The time of the Elves is over.
My people are leaving these shores.

942
01:31:23,979 --> 01:31:27,597
Who will you look to when we've gone?
The Dwarves?

943
01:31:27,691 --> 01:31:32,856
They hide in mountains seeking riches.
They care not for the troubles of others.

944
01:31:34,489 --> 01:31:37,322
It is in Men
that we must place our hope.

945
01:31:37,659 --> 01:31:39,365
Men?

946
01:31:40,245 --> 01:31:43,533
Men are weak.
The race of Men is failing.

947
01:31:43,623 --> 01:31:48,117
The blood of Númenor is all but spent,
its pride and dignity forgotten.

948
01:31:48,420 --> 01:31:52,004
It is because of Men
the Ring survives.

949
01:31:52,090 --> 01:31:53,751
I was there, Gandalf.

950
01:31:54,426 --> 01:31:57,259
<i>I was there 3000 years ago...</i>

951
01:32:04,102 --> 01:32:06,559
<i>...when Isildur took the Ring.</i>

952
01:32:06,646 --> 01:32:10,605
I was there the day
the strength of Men failed.

953
01:32:13,153 --> 01:32:15,690
Isildur, hurry! Follow me.

954
01:32:17,282 --> 01:32:20,900
ELROND: <i>I led Isildur into the heart</i>
<i>of Mount Doom...</i>

955
01:32:21,161 --> 01:32:24,745
<i>...where the Ring was forged,</i>
<i>the one place it could be destroyed.</i>

956
01:32:24,831 --> 01:32:27,447
Cast it into the fire!

957
01:32:27,792 --> 01:32:30,625
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

958
01:32:32,630 --> 01:32:36,418
-Destroy it!
-No.

959
01:32:37,761 --> 01:32:39,922
Isildur!

960
01:32:40,388 --> 01:32:45,132
ELROND: <i>It should have ended that day,</i>
<i>but evil was allowed to endure.</i>

961
01:32:49,230 --> 01:32:53,473
Isildur kept the Ring.
The line of kings is broken.

962
01:32:54,402 --> 01:32:58,111
There's no strength left
in the world of Men.

963
01:32:58,198 --> 01:33:03,158
-They're scattered, divided, leaderless.
-There is one who could unite them.

964
01:33:03,244 --> 01:33:06,657
One who could reclaim
the throne of Gondor.

965
01:33:08,333 --> 01:33:12,201
He turned from that path
a long time ago.

966
01:33:12,295 --> 01:33:14,456
He has chosen exile.

967
01:33:45,703 --> 01:33:47,739
You are no Elf.

968
01:33:47,831 --> 01:33:49,947
Men of the South are welcome here.

969
01:33:50,542 --> 01:33:54,034
-Who are you?
-I am a friend to Gandalf the Grey.

970
01:33:55,547 --> 01:33:58,380
Then we are here on common purpose...

971
01:33:58,758 --> 01:34:00,214
...friend.

972
01:34:15,400 --> 01:34:18,312
The shards of Narsil.

973
01:34:21,781 --> 01:34:26,241
The blade that cut the Ring
from Sauron's hand.

974
01:34:29,164 --> 01:34:31,405
It's still sharp.

975
01:34:40,300 --> 01:34:43,383
But no more than a broken heirloom.

976
01:35:10,205 --> 01:35:13,242
Why do you fear the past?

977
01:35:14,125 --> 01:35:19,461
You are Isildur's heir,
not Isildur himself.

978
01:35:19,714 --> 01:35:23,127
You are not bound to his fate.

979
01:35:23,635 --> 01:35:27,628
The same blood flows in my veins.

980
01:35:30,642 --> 01:35:33,224
The same weakness.

981
01:35:35,939 --> 01:35:38,806
Your time will come.

982
01:35:38,900 --> 01:35:43,314
You will face the same evil.
And you will defeat it.

983
01:35:46,491 --> 01:35:48,903
[IN ELVISH]

984
01:36:11,641 --> 01:36:16,180
[IN ELVISH]

985
01:36:33,871 --> 01:36:36,533
[IN ENGLISH]
You said you'd bind yourself to me...

986
01:36:38,543 --> 01:36:43,537
...forsaking the immortal life
of your people.

987
01:36:44,674 --> 01:36:46,585
[IN ENGLISH]
And to that I hold.

988
01:36:46,676 --> 01:36:50,339
I would rather share
one lifetime with you...

989
01:36:50,596 --> 01:36:54,464
...than face all the Ages
of this world alone.

990
01:37:03,234 --> 01:37:06,692
I choose a mortal life.

991
01:37:08,031 --> 01:37:12,274
-You cannot give me this.
-It is mine to give to whom I will...

992
01:37:15,538 --> 01:37:18,029
...like my heart.

993
01:37:33,806 --> 01:37:37,594
ELROND: Strangers from distant lands,
friends of old...

994
01:37:37,685 --> 01:37:41,644
...you've been summoned here
to answer the threat of Mordor.

995
01:37:42,273 --> 01:37:47,142
Middle-earth stands upon the brink
of destruction. None can escape it.

996
01:37:47,403 --> 01:37:50,987
You will unite, or you will fall.

997
01:37:51,074 --> 01:37:55,408
Each race is bound to this fate,
this one doom.

998
01:37:57,246 --> 01:38:00,738
Bring forth the Ring, Frodo.

999
01:38:14,806 --> 01:38:16,546
So it is true.

1000
01:38:33,991 --> 01:38:36,107
In a dream...

1001
01:38:37,703 --> 01:38:40,820
...I saw the eastern sky grow dark...

1002
01:38:41,124 --> 01:38:42,830
...but in the West
a pale light lingered.

1003
01:38:43,626 --> 01:38:45,366
A voice was crying:

1004
01:38:45,670 --> 01:38:48,582
"Your doom is near at hand.

1005
01:38:49,590 --> 01:38:52,332
Isildur's Bane is found."

1006
01:38:56,347 --> 01:38:58,178
Isildur's Bane.

1007
01:38:58,850 --> 01:39:00,215
Boromir!

1008
01:39:00,309 --> 01:39:03,972
[GANDALF CHANTS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1009
01:39:04,480 --> 01:39:08,018
[VOICE OF THE RING
ECHOES IN BLACK SPEECH]

1010
01:39:23,332 --> 01:39:27,200
Never before has any voice uttered the
words of that tongue here in Imladris.

1011
01:39:27,295 --> 01:39:31,083
I do not ask your pardon,
Master Elrond...

1012
01:39:31,174 --> 01:39:33,335
...for the Black Speech of Mordor...

1013
01:39:33,634 --> 01:39:35,044
...may yet be heard...

1014
01:39:35,136 --> 01:39:38,219
...in every corner of the West!

1015
01:39:38,306 --> 01:39:41,013
The Ring is altogether evil.

1016
01:39:41,350 --> 01:39:42,840
It is a gift.

1017
01:39:43,436 --> 01:39:45,518
A gift to the foes of Mordor.

1018
01:39:46,147 --> 01:39:48,308
Why not use this Ring?

1019
01:39:48,399 --> 01:39:51,266
Long has my father,
the Steward of Gondor...

1020
01:39:51,360 --> 01:39:55,729
...kept the forces of Mordor at bay.
By the blood of our people...

1021
01:39:56,032 --> 01:39:58,239
...are your lands kept safe.

1022
01:40:00,036 --> 01:40:04,370
Give Gondor the weapon of the enemy.
Let us use it against him.

1023
01:40:04,665 --> 01:40:08,408
You cannot wield it.
None of us can.

1024
01:40:09,045 --> 01:40:13,129
The One Ring answers to Sauron alone.
It has no other master.

1025
01:40:13,216 --> 01:40:16,800
And what would a Ranger know
of this matter?

1026
01:40:17,094 --> 01:40:19,085
This is no mere Ranger.

1027
01:40:20,097 --> 01:40:23,760
He is Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

1028
01:40:24,268 --> 01:40:27,180
You owe him your allegiance.

1029
01:40:31,275 --> 01:40:33,186
Aragorn.

1030
01:40:34,946 --> 01:40:37,779
This is Isildur's heir?

1031
01:40:40,117 --> 01:40:42,824
And heir to the throne of Gondor.

1032
01:40:44,956 --> 01:40:46,412
[IN ELVISH]

1033
01:40:49,794 --> 01:40:52,627
Gondor has no king.

1034
01:40:54,465 --> 01:40:56,126
Gondor needs no king.

1035
01:41:02,807 --> 01:41:06,470
Aragorn is right. We cannot use it.

1036
01:41:07,478 --> 01:41:10,970
You have only one choice.

1037
01:41:11,232 --> 01:41:13,598
The Ring must be destroyed.

1038
01:41:15,444 --> 01:41:18,527
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1039
01:41:18,823 --> 01:41:21,360
What are we waiting for?

1040
01:41:27,290 --> 01:41:31,499
[VOICE OF THE RING
SPEAKS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1041
01:41:33,504 --> 01:41:36,496
The Ring cannot be destroyed, Gimli,
son of Glóin...

1042
01:41:36,757 --> 01:41:41,000
...by any craft that we here possess.

1043
01:41:41,512 --> 01:41:45,721
The Ring was made in the fires
of Mount Doom.

1044
01:41:45,808 --> 01:41:49,676
Only there can it be unmade.

1045
01:41:50,730 --> 01:41:53,392
It must be taken deep into Mordor...

1046
01:41:53,482 --> 01:41:57,350
...and cast back into the fiery chasm
from whence it came.

1047
01:41:57,445 --> 01:41:59,276
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1048
01:42:00,531 --> 01:42:02,522
One of you...

1049
01:42:03,034 --> 01:42:05,195
...must do this.

1050
01:42:08,122 --> 01:42:11,831
One does not simply walk into Mordor.

1051
01:42:12,710 --> 01:42:16,373
Its Black Gates are guarded
by more than just Orcs.

1052
01:42:17,214 --> 01:42:21,423
There is evil there
that does not sleep.

1053
01:42:21,510 --> 01:42:25,753
The Great Eye is ever-watchful.

1054
01:42:26,557 --> 01:42:28,639
It is a barren wasteland...

1055
01:42:28,726 --> 01:42:32,435
...riddled with fire, and ash
and dust.

1056
01:42:32,521 --> 01:42:36,389
The very air you breathe
is a poisonous fume.

1057
01:42:36,651 --> 01:42:40,894
Not with 10,000 men
could you do this. It is folly.

1058
01:42:41,155 --> 01:42:45,649
Have you heard nothing Lord Elrond
has said? The Ring must be destroyed.

1059
01:42:45,743 --> 01:42:48,450
And I suppose you think
you are the one to do it!

1060
01:42:48,537 --> 01:42:53,281
And if we fail, what then? What happens
when Sauron takes back what is his?

1061
01:42:53,376 --> 01:42:58,791
I will be dead before I see the Ring
in the hands of an Elf!

1062
01:42:58,881 --> 01:43:00,621
[SHOUTING]

1063
01:43:00,716 --> 01:43:03,253
Never trust an Elf!

1064
01:43:04,428 --> 01:43:10,264
GANDALF: Do you not understand?
While you bicker, Sauron's power grows!

1065
01:43:10,601 --> 01:43:13,434
None can escape it!
You'll all be destroyed!

1066
01:43:14,772 --> 01:43:18,435
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1067
01:43:32,248 --> 01:43:34,455
I will take it.

1068
01:43:36,460 --> 01:43:38,951
I will take it.

1069
01:43:44,802 --> 01:43:47,839
I will take the Ring to Mordor.

1070
01:43:55,896 --> 01:43:57,136
Though...

1071
01:44:00,234 --> 01:44:02,065
...I do not know the way.

1072
01:44:04,071 --> 01:44:08,440
I will help you bear
this burden, Frodo Baggins...

1073
01:44:08,534 --> 01:44:11,947
...as long as it is yours to bear.

1074
01:44:13,080 --> 01:44:16,163
If by my life
or death I can protect you...

1075
01:44:16,917 --> 01:44:18,248
...I will.

1076
01:44:21,464 --> 01:44:23,750
You have my sword.

1077
01:44:25,593 --> 01:44:27,675
And you have my bow.

1078
01:44:28,262 --> 01:44:30,753
And my ax.

1079
01:44:37,772 --> 01:44:40,764
You carry the fates
of us all, little one.

1080
01:44:42,777 --> 01:44:46,440
If this is indeed
the will of the Council...

1081
01:44:46,906 --> 01:44:49,318
-...then Gondor will see it done.
-Hey!

1082
01:44:51,952 --> 01:44:56,787
-Frodo's not going anywhere without me.
-It is hardly possible to separate you...

1083
01:44:56,874 --> 01:45:01,789
...even when he is summoned
to a secret Council and you are not.

1084
01:45:02,296 --> 01:45:04,252
We're coming too!

1085
01:45:06,383 --> 01:45:09,125
You'll have to send us home
tied up in a sack to stop us.

1086
01:45:09,386 --> 01:45:12,719
Anyway, you need people
of intelligence on this sort of...

1087
01:45:13,057 --> 01:45:14,422
...mission.

1088
01:45:14,517 --> 01:45:16,053
Quest.

1089
01:45:16,519 --> 01:45:17,554
Thing.

1090
01:45:19,396 --> 01:45:22,058
Well, that rules you out, Pip.

1091
01:45:23,651 --> 01:45:25,562
Nine companions.

1092
01:45:27,404 --> 01:45:29,235
So be it.

1093
01:45:29,573 --> 01:45:32,565
You shall be
the Fellowship of the Ring.

1094
01:45:33,244 --> 01:45:35,155
Great!

1095
01:45:35,246 --> 01:45:37,578
Where are we going?

1096
01:46:19,957 --> 01:46:22,494
ELROND [IN ELVISH]:

1097
01:46:24,420 --> 01:46:28,208
ELROND [IN ELVISH]:

1098
01:46:30,634 --> 01:46:34,126
[IN ENGLISH] In her heart, your mother
knew you'd be hunted all your life.

1099
01:46:34,638 --> 01:46:36,299
That you'd never escape your fate.

1100
01:46:36,807 --> 01:46:40,470
The skill of the Elves
can reforge the sword of kings...

1101
01:46:40,895 --> 01:46:44,808
...but only you have the power
to wield it.

1102
01:46:45,816 --> 01:46:48,307
I do not want that power.

1103
01:46:48,485 --> 01:46:51,147
I have never wanted it.

1104
01:46:52,489 --> 01:46:55,105
You are the last of that bloodline.
There is no other.

1105
01:46:59,496 --> 01:47:01,828
BILBO:
My old sword! Sting.

1106
01:47:02,041 --> 01:47:03,156
Here, take it. Take it.

1107
01:47:08,672 --> 01:47:12,631
-It's so light.
-Yes. Made by the Elves, you know.

1108
01:47:13,344 --> 01:47:17,428
The blade glows blue
when Orcs are close.

1109
01:47:17,640 --> 01:47:22,179
And it's times like that, my lad,
when you have to be extra careful.

1110
01:47:22,394 --> 01:47:24,851
Here's a pretty thing.

1111
01:47:25,272 --> 01:47:26,557
Mithril.

1112
01:47:27,358 --> 01:47:31,727
As light as a feather,
and as hard as dragon scales.

1113
01:47:31,946 --> 01:47:35,188
Let me see you put it on. Come on.

1114
01:47:38,744 --> 01:47:40,200
Oh!

1115
01:47:43,248 --> 01:47:45,284
My old ring.

1116
01:47:46,543 --> 01:47:50,456
I should very much like...

1117
01:47:50,714 --> 01:47:54,707
...to hold it again, one last time.

1118
01:48:12,069 --> 01:48:15,732
I'm sorry I brought this upon you,
my boy.

1119
01:48:16,073 --> 01:48:20,191
I'm sorry that you
must carry this burden.

1120
01:48:24,707 --> 01:48:27,744
I'm sorry for everything.

1121
01:48:42,766 --> 01:48:46,975
The Ring-bearer is setting out
on the Quest of Mount Doom.

1122
01:48:48,313 --> 01:48:50,929
On you who travel with him,
no oath...

1123
01:48:51,150 --> 01:48:54,267
...nor bond is laid to go further
than you will.

1124
01:48:57,740 --> 01:49:00,277
Farewell. Hold to your purpose.

1125
01:49:00,743 --> 01:49:04,656
May the blessings of Elves and Men...

1126
01:49:05,205 --> 01:49:07,787
...and all Free Folk go with you.

1127
01:49:10,878 --> 01:49:14,962
The Fellowship awaits the Ring-bearer.

1128
01:49:33,400 --> 01:49:35,891
Mordor, Gandalf, is it left or right?

1129
01:49:36,445 --> 01:49:38,276
Left.

1130
01:50:57,776 --> 01:51:02,190
GANDALF: <i>We must hold to this course,</i>
<i>west of the Misty Mountains, for 40 days.</i>

1131
01:51:02,406 --> 01:51:06,149
<i>If our luck holds, the Gap of Rohan</i>
<i>will still be open to us.</i>

1132
01:51:06,368 --> 01:51:09,906
<i>From there, our road</i>
<i>turns east to Mordor.</i>

1133
01:51:10,080 --> 01:51:13,914
Two, one, five. Good! Very good.

1134
01:51:15,752 --> 01:51:16,787
Move your feet.

1135
01:51:17,004 --> 01:51:18,335
MERRY: You look good, Pippin.
-Thanks.

1136
01:51:18,547 --> 01:51:19,912
BOROMIR:
Faster!

1137
01:51:21,300 --> 01:51:25,088
If anyone was to ask for my opinion,
which I note they're not...

1138
01:51:25,304 --> 01:51:28,046
...I'd say we were taking
the long way 'round.

1139
01:51:28,557 --> 01:51:31,594
Gandalf, we could pass through
the Mines of Moria.

1140
01:51:32,269 --> 01:51:36,103
My cousin Balin would give us
a royal welcome.

1141
01:51:36,440 --> 01:51:41,810
No, I would not take the road through
Moria unless I had no other choice.

1142
01:51:51,038 --> 01:51:52,118
Sorry!

1143
01:51:52,956 --> 01:51:54,446
MERRY:
Get him!

1144
01:51:55,792 --> 01:51:58,249
MERRY: For the Shire!
PIPPIN: Hold him. Hold him down, Merry!

1145
01:51:58,795 --> 01:52:01,127
Gentlemen, that's enough.

1146
01:52:04,927 --> 01:52:06,542
MERRY: You've got my arm!
You've got my arm!

1147
01:52:06,970 --> 01:52:09,632
-What is that?
-Nothing. It's just a wisp of cloud.

1148
01:52:09,890 --> 01:52:12,597
It's moving fast.

1149
01:52:12,809 --> 01:52:14,970
Against the wind.

1150
01:52:15,771 --> 01:52:17,887
-Crebain from Dunland!
-Hide!

1151
01:52:18,106 --> 01:52:20,813
-Hurry!
-Take cover!

1152
01:52:54,226 --> 01:52:55,966
Spies of Saruman.

1153
01:52:56,728 --> 01:53:00,016
The passage south is being watched.

1154
01:53:01,191 --> 01:53:04,524
We must take the Pass of Caradhras.

1155
01:53:17,165 --> 01:53:18,871
ARAGORN:
Frodo!

1156
01:53:37,853 --> 01:53:40,094
Boromir.

1157
01:53:40,355 --> 01:53:44,564
It is a strange fate that we should
suffer so much fear and doubt...

1158
01:53:44,776 --> 01:53:47,893
...over so small a thing.

1159
01:53:51,116 --> 01:53:53,072
Such a little thing.

1160
01:53:53,285 --> 01:53:54,741
Boromir!

1161
01:53:55,370 --> 01:53:58,077
Give the Ring to Frodo.

1162
01:54:07,883 --> 01:54:09,919
As you wish.

1163
01:54:10,635 --> 01:54:12,626
I care not.

1164
01:54:17,100 --> 01:54:19,432
[BOROMIR CHUCKLES]

1165
01:54:29,821 --> 01:54:32,608
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

1166
01:54:48,048 --> 01:54:52,758
So, Gandalf, you try
to lead them over Caradhras.

1167
01:54:52,969 --> 01:54:57,554
And if that fails,
where then will you go?

1168
01:54:58,850 --> 01:55:01,808
<i>If the mountain defeats you...</i>

1169
01:55:02,062 --> 01:55:06,476
<i>...will you risk</i>
<i>a more dangerous road?</i>

1170
01:55:12,989 --> 01:55:15,651
[SARUMAN CHANTS IN QUENYA]

1171
01:55:18,829 --> 01:55:21,696
There is a fell voice on the air.

1172
01:55:22,833 --> 01:55:24,323
It's Saruman!

1173
01:55:33,218 --> 01:55:37,882
He's trying to bring down the mountain!
Gandalf, we must turn back!

1174
01:55:38,181 --> 01:55:39,967
No!

1175
01:55:42,978 --> 01:55:45,811
[CHANTS IN SINDARIN]

1176
01:56:46,416 --> 01:56:48,247
We must get off the mountain!

1177
01:56:48,752 --> 01:56:53,086
Make for the Gap of Rohan,
and take the west road to my city!

1178
01:56:53,256 --> 01:56:56,589
The Gap of Rohan takes us
too close to Isengard!

1179
01:56:56,760 --> 01:57:00,503
GIMLI: We cannot pass over a mountain.
Let us go under it.

1180
01:57:00,764 --> 01:57:03,597
Let us go through the Mines of Moria.

1181
01:57:05,435 --> 01:57:09,269
SARUMAN: <i>Moria. You fear to go</i>
<i>into those mines.</i>

1182
01:57:09,940 --> 01:57:14,934
The Dwarves delved too greedily
and too deep.

1183
01:57:15,779 --> 01:57:20,648
<i>You know what they awoke</i>
<i>in the darkness of Khazad-dûm:</i>

1184
01:57:21,952 --> 01:57:25,444
Shadow and flame.

1185
01:57:28,792 --> 01:57:31,454
Let the Ring-bearer decide.

1186
01:57:36,174 --> 01:57:38,290
We cannot stay here!

1187
01:57:38,468 --> 01:57:41,301
This will be the death of the Hobbits.

1188
01:57:41,471 --> 01:57:43,177
Frodo?

1189
01:57:46,184 --> 01:57:49,051
We will go through the mines.

1190
01:57:49,813 --> 01:57:51,678
So be it.

1191
01:57:58,321 --> 01:58:02,280
Frodo, come and help an old man.

1192
01:58:05,829 --> 01:58:07,990
How is your shoulder?

1193
01:58:08,206 --> 01:58:11,494
-Better than it was.
-And the Ring?

1194
01:58:13,003 --> 01:58:15,494
You feel its power growing, don't you?

1195
01:58:16,006 --> 01:58:18,918
I've felt it too.
You must be careful now.

1196
01:58:19,342 --> 01:58:23,255
Evil will be drawn to you
from outside the Fellowship.

1197
01:58:23,430 --> 01:58:26,012
And, I fear, from within.

1198
01:58:28,685 --> 01:58:32,849
-Who then do I trust?
-You must trust yourself.

1199
01:58:33,023 --> 01:58:35,856
Trust your own strengths.

1200
01:58:36,026 --> 01:58:38,608
-What do you mean?
-There are many powers in this world...

1201
01:58:38,820 --> 01:58:40,856
...for good or for evil.

1202
01:58:41,031 --> 01:58:43,363
Some are greater than I am.

1203
01:58:43,867 --> 01:58:47,530
And against some I have not yet
been tested.

1204
01:58:48,872 --> 01:58:50,237
The walls...

1205
01:58:50,957 --> 01:58:53,039
...of Moria.

1206
01:58:58,757 --> 01:59:01,749
Dwarf doors are invisible when closed.

1207
01:59:01,968 --> 01:59:06,382
GANDALF: Their own masters cannot find
them if their secrets are forgotten.

1208
01:59:06,765 --> 01:59:09,256
Why doesn't that surprise me?

1209
01:59:17,275 --> 01:59:20,563
Well, let's see.

1210
01:59:20,779 --> 01:59:22,144
Ithildin.

1211
01:59:22,781 --> 01:59:26,148
It mirrors only starlight
and moonlight.

1212
01:59:40,215 --> 01:59:44,299
It reads, "The Doors of Durin,
Lord of Moria.

1213
01:59:44,886 --> 01:59:49,505
-Speak, friend, and enter."
-What do you suppose that means?

1214
01:59:49,766 --> 01:59:54,510
It's simple. If you are a friend, you speak
the password and the doors will open.

1215
01:59:55,063 --> 01:59:58,521
[GANDALF SPEAKS IN ELVISH]

1216
02:00:18,294 --> 02:00:19,409
Nothing's happening.

1217
02:00:26,428 --> 02:00:30,637
I once knew every spell
in all the tongues of Elves...

1218
02:00:30,974 --> 02:00:33,807
...Men and Orcs.

1219
02:00:34,060 --> 02:00:35,300
What are you going to do, then?

1220
02:00:35,478 --> 02:00:37,719
Knock your head against these doors,
Peregrin Took!

1221
02:00:37,981 --> 02:00:39,972
And if that does not shatter them...

1222
02:00:40,150 --> 02:00:42,857
...and I am allowed a little peace
from foolish questions...

1223
02:00:43,027 --> 02:00:46,485
...I will try to find the opening words.

1224
02:00:46,948 --> 02:00:50,816
[GANDALF SPEAKS IN ELVISH
AND DWARVISH]

1225
02:00:59,335 --> 02:01:01,872
Mines are no place for a pony.

1226
02:01:02,088 --> 02:01:06,172
-Even one so brave as Bill.
-Bye-bye, Bill.

1227
02:01:07,343 --> 02:01:10,176
Go on, Bill. Go on.

1228
02:01:10,680 --> 02:01:14,218
Don't worry, Sam,
he knows the way home.

1229
02:01:21,024 --> 02:01:23,606
Do not disturb the water.

1230
02:01:23,860 --> 02:01:25,691
Oh, it's useless.

1231
02:01:38,374 --> 02:01:40,535
It's a riddle.

1232
02:01:43,296 --> 02:01:46,413
"Speak 'friend' and enter."

1233
02:01:46,800 --> 02:01:49,712
What's the Elvish word for "friend"?

1234
02:01:51,221 --> 02:01:52,506
<i>Mellon.</i>

1235
02:02:10,573 --> 02:02:15,408
GIMLI: Soon, Master Elf, you will enjoy
the fabled hospitality of the Dwarves.

1236
02:02:15,912 --> 02:02:21,578
Roaring fires, malt beer,
ripe meat off the bone!

1237
02:02:23,086 --> 02:02:26,169
This, my friend,
is the home of my cousin Balin.

1238
02:02:26,548 --> 02:02:28,914
And they call it a mine.

1239
02:02:29,133 --> 02:02:31,089
A mine!

1240
02:02:32,136 --> 02:02:35,469
This is no mine. It's a tomb.

1241
02:02:39,769 --> 02:02:41,179
GIMLI:
No.

1242
02:02:41,604 --> 02:02:43,185
No....

1243
02:02:44,440 --> 02:02:46,101
No!

1244
02:02:48,778 --> 02:02:50,268
Goblins.

1245
02:02:54,200 --> 02:02:58,489
We make for the Gap of Rohan.
We should never have come here.

1246
02:02:59,581 --> 02:03:02,118
ARAGORN:
Now, get out of here. Get out!

1247
02:03:04,961 --> 02:03:07,293
MERRY: Frodo!
FRODO: Help!

1248
02:03:07,505 --> 02:03:09,120
Strider!

1249
02:03:09,299 --> 02:03:12,132
FRODO: Help!
SAM: Get off him!

1250
02:03:12,302 --> 02:03:13,291
Aragorn!

1251
02:03:23,730 --> 02:03:24,810
Frodo!

1252
02:03:25,982 --> 02:03:27,518
Strider!

1253
02:03:51,132 --> 02:03:52,167
Into the mines!

1254
02:03:52,342 --> 02:03:55,550
-Legolas!
ARAGORN: Into the cave!

1255
02:03:59,849 --> 02:04:01,635
Run!

1256
02:04:18,534 --> 02:04:22,072
GANDALF:
We now have but one choice.

1257
02:04:22,288 --> 02:04:27,203
We must face the long dark of Moria.

1258
02:04:27,418 --> 02:04:29,374
Be on your guard.

1259
02:04:29,587 --> 02:04:33,045
There are older
and fouler things than Orcs...

1260
02:04:33,216 --> 02:04:36,754
...in the deep places of the world.

1261
02:04:44,727 --> 02:04:48,686
Quietly now. It's a four-day journey
to the other side.

1262
02:04:48,898 --> 02:04:52,732
Let us hope that our presence
may go unnoticed.

1263
02:05:38,489 --> 02:05:42,198
The wealth of Moria is not in gold...

1264
02:05:42,368 --> 02:05:44,780
...or jewels...

1265
02:05:44,954 --> 02:05:47,991
...but mithril.

1266
02:06:06,350 --> 02:06:11,265
Bilbo had a shirt of mithril rings
that Thorin gave him.

1267
02:06:11,481 --> 02:06:15,474
-Oh, that was a kingly gift.
-Yes.

1268
02:06:15,651 --> 02:06:17,516
I never told him...

1269
02:06:17,695 --> 02:06:22,655
...but its worth was greater than
the value of the Shire.

1270
02:06:35,004 --> 02:06:36,710
Pippin.

1271
02:06:57,401 --> 02:07:00,017
I have no memory of this place.

1272
02:07:02,115 --> 02:07:03,605
PIPPIN: Are we lost?
MERRY: No.

1273
02:07:03,825 --> 02:07:06,316
PIPPIN: I think we are.
MERRY: Gandalf's thinking.

1274
02:07:06,536 --> 02:07:07,946
PIPPIN: Merry?
MERRY: What?

1275
02:07:08,246 --> 02:07:10,202
PIPPIN:
I'm hungry.

1276
02:07:21,509 --> 02:07:25,969
-There's something down there.
-It's Gollum.

1277
02:07:26,180 --> 02:07:30,298
-Gollum?
-He's been following us for three days.

1278
02:07:30,518 --> 02:07:34,682
-He escaped the dungeons of Barad-dûr?
-Escaped...

1279
02:07:35,356 --> 02:07:37,017
...or was set loose.

1280
02:07:37,525 --> 02:07:41,188
Now the Ring has brought him here.

1281
02:07:43,823 --> 02:07:46,565
He will never be rid of his need for it.

1282
02:07:46,742 --> 02:07:52,487
He hates and loves the Ring,
as he hates and loves himself.

1283
02:07:52,665 --> 02:07:57,534
Sméagol's life is a sad story.

1284
02:07:57,712 --> 02:08:03,673
Yes, Sméagol he was once called.
Before the Ring found him.

1285
02:08:04,594 --> 02:08:07,381
Before it drove him mad.

1286
02:08:07,680 --> 02:08:10,547
It's a pity Bilbo didn't kill him
when he had the chance.

1287
02:08:10,725 --> 02:08:11,931
Pity?

1288
02:08:13,019 --> 02:08:15,886
It is pity that stayed Bilbo's hand.

1289
02:08:16,814 --> 02:08:22,025
Many that live deserve death.
Some that die deserve life.

1290
02:08:23,446 --> 02:08:25,937
Can you give it to them, Frodo?

1291
02:08:28,367 --> 02:08:32,326
Do not be too eager
to deal out death and judgment.

1292
02:08:32,538 --> 02:08:35,450
Even the very wise
cannot see all ends.

1293
02:08:36,042 --> 02:08:41,958
My heart tells me that Gollum has some
part to play yet, for good or ill...

1294
02:08:42,757 --> 02:08:45,590
...before this is over.

1295
02:08:47,094 --> 02:08:50,962
The pity of Bilbo
may rule the fate of many.

1296
02:08:57,605 --> 02:09:00,972
I wish the Ring
had never come to me.

1297
02:09:02,401 --> 02:09:04,437
I wish none of this had happened.

1298
02:09:04,612 --> 02:09:09,652
So do all who live to see such times.
But that is not for them to decide.

1299
02:09:10,493 --> 02:09:15,988
All we have to decide is what to do
with the time that is given to us.

1300
02:09:17,500 --> 02:09:21,493
There are other forces at work in this
world, Frodo, besides the will of evil.

1301
02:09:21,879 --> 02:09:24,291
Bilbo was meant to find the Ring.

1302
02:09:24,799 --> 02:09:29,133
In which case,
you also were meant to have it.

1303
02:09:29,303 --> 02:09:32,511
And that is an encouraging thought.

1304
02:09:35,434 --> 02:09:36,594
Ah!

1305
02:09:37,395 --> 02:09:39,306
It's that way.

1306
02:09:39,522 --> 02:09:41,808
-He's remembered.
GANDALF: No.

1307
02:09:42,024 --> 02:09:45,812
But the air doesn't smell
so foul down here.

1308
02:09:46,028 --> 02:09:51,193
If in doubt, Meriadoc,
always follow your nose.

1309
02:10:06,048 --> 02:10:10,166
Let me risk a little more light.

1310
02:10:14,849 --> 02:10:16,931
Behold...

1311
02:10:17,351 --> 02:10:22,562
...the great realm
and Dwarf-city of Dwarrowdelf.

1312
02:10:25,067 --> 02:10:28,480
There's an eye opener, and no mistake.

1313
02:10:53,387 --> 02:10:55,093
Gimli!

1314
02:11:00,895 --> 02:11:02,351
No.

1315
02:11:02,563 --> 02:11:04,178
No!

1316
02:11:06,734 --> 02:11:09,897
Oh, no.

1317
02:11:11,739 --> 02:11:13,024
No.

1318
02:11:20,289 --> 02:11:22,280
GANDALF:
"Here lies Balin...

1319
02:11:22,750 --> 02:11:24,741
...son of Fundin...

1320
02:11:25,086 --> 02:11:27,702
...Lord of Moria."

1321
02:11:28,756 --> 02:11:30,417
He is dead, then.

1322
02:11:32,593 --> 02:11:33,799
It's as I feared.

1323
02:11:45,106 --> 02:11:46,812
[GIMLI SPEAKS DWARVISH]

1324
02:11:52,113 --> 02:11:55,025
We must move on. We cannot linger.

1325
02:11:55,241 --> 02:11:59,951
GANDALF: "They have taken the bridge
and the second hall.

1326
02:12:01,038 --> 02:12:03,620
We have barred the gates...

1327
02:12:04,291 --> 02:12:06,782
...but cannot hold them for long.

1328
02:12:06,961 --> 02:12:09,794
The ground shakes.

1329
02:12:10,172 --> 02:12:11,787
Drums...

1330
02:12:12,174 --> 02:12:15,541
...drums in the deep.

1331
02:12:19,098 --> 02:12:21,134
We cannot get out.

1332
02:12:23,144 --> 02:12:26,978
A Shadow moves in the dark.

1333
02:12:28,649 --> 02:12:31,186
We cannot get out.

1334
02:12:34,196 --> 02:12:36,152
They are coming."

1335
02:12:39,368 --> 02:12:41,199
[CLATTERING]

1336
02:12:58,596 --> 02:13:01,884
[THUDDING]

1337
02:13:07,813 --> 02:13:09,553
[SILENCE]

1338
02:13:19,200 --> 02:13:21,031
Fool of a Took!

1339
02:13:21,368 --> 02:13:25,202
Throw yourself in next time,
and rid us of your stupidity.

1340
02:13:28,834 --> 02:13:31,701
[DRUMS BEATING]

1341
02:13:41,931 --> 02:13:44,263
[SCREECHING]

1342
02:13:51,148 --> 02:13:52,763
SAM:
Frodo!

1343
02:13:55,069 --> 02:13:56,559
Orcs.

1344
02:14:03,619 --> 02:14:05,610
Get back! Stay close to Gandalf!

1345
02:14:12,878 --> 02:14:14,664
They have a cave-troll.

1346
02:14:30,479 --> 02:14:31,639
Let them come!

1347
02:14:32,147 --> 02:14:35,685
There is one Dwarf yet in Moria
who still draws breath.

1348
02:14:50,833 --> 02:14:52,698
[SCREECHES]

1349
02:16:54,581 --> 02:16:57,323
I think I'm getting the hang of this.

1350
02:17:02,089 --> 02:17:03,750
Frodo!

1351
02:17:37,291 --> 02:17:39,122
FRODO:
Aragorn! Aragorn!

1352
02:17:40,127 --> 02:17:41,992
Frodo!

1353
02:18:27,174 --> 02:18:29,039
Frodo!

1354
02:18:31,845 --> 02:18:33,301
Frodo!

1355
02:19:29,278 --> 02:19:30,609
Oh, no.

1356
02:19:33,448 --> 02:19:34,904
[FRODO GROANS]

1357
02:19:38,996 --> 02:19:40,861
He's alive.

1358
02:19:43,292 --> 02:19:46,284
I'm all right. I'm not hurt.

1359
02:19:46,628 --> 02:19:48,789
You should be dead.

1360
02:19:49,006 --> 02:19:51,497
That spear would have skewered
a wild boar.

1361
02:19:51,758 --> 02:19:56,502
I think there's more to this Hobbit
than meets the eye.

1362
02:20:02,311 --> 02:20:03,426
Mithril.

1363
02:20:06,231 --> 02:20:08,813
You are full of surprises,
Master Baggins.

1364
02:20:09,318 --> 02:20:12,276
[SCREECHING]

1365
02:20:14,823 --> 02:20:16,779
To the Bridge of Khazad-dûm!

1366
02:20:31,757 --> 02:20:33,338
ARAGORN:
This way!

1367
02:21:16,969 --> 02:21:19,005
[GROWLING]

1368
02:21:43,745 --> 02:21:46,737
What is this new devilry?

1369
02:22:00,887 --> 02:22:02,673
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1370
02:22:02,848 --> 02:22:05,635
A Balrog.

1371
02:22:05,934 --> 02:22:09,097
A demon of the ancient world.

1372
02:22:11,273 --> 02:22:13,730
This foe is beyond any of you.

1373
02:22:14,901 --> 02:22:16,437
Run!

1374
02:22:23,785 --> 02:22:25,275
Quickly!

1375
02:22:41,928 --> 02:22:43,168
Gandalf.

1376
02:22:43,805 --> 02:22:45,420
Lead them on, Aragorn.

1377
02:22:46,808 --> 02:22:49,299
The bridge is near.

1378
02:22:49,561 --> 02:22:51,176
[BALROG GROWLS]

1379
02:22:51,396 --> 02:22:55,480
Do as I say!
Swords are no more use here.

1380
02:23:24,638 --> 02:23:26,344
Gandalf!

1381
02:23:44,658 --> 02:23:45,864
BOROMIR:
Merry! Pippin!

1382
02:23:57,003 --> 02:23:58,539
Sam!

1383
02:24:01,258 --> 02:24:04,500
Nobody tosses a Dwarf.

1384
02:24:07,556 --> 02:24:08,966
Not the beard!

1385
02:24:22,195 --> 02:24:24,060
Steady.

1386
02:24:26,199 --> 02:24:27,860
Hold on!

1387
02:24:30,829 --> 02:24:32,694
[BALROG GROWLS]

1388
02:24:33,790 --> 02:24:35,701
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1389
02:24:48,930 --> 02:24:50,090
Hang on!

1390
02:25:00,901 --> 02:25:02,607
Lean forward!

1391
02:25:05,614 --> 02:25:06,603
Steady.

1392
02:25:07,949 --> 02:25:09,109
Come on!

1393
02:25:09,367 --> 02:25:10,857
Now!

1394
02:25:28,094 --> 02:25:29,880
Over the bridge!

1395
02:25:30,138 --> 02:25:31,628
Fly!

1396
02:26:16,351 --> 02:26:18,342
You cannot pass!

1397
02:26:18,520 --> 02:26:20,181
Gandalf!

1398
02:26:24,401 --> 02:26:29,270
I am a servant of the Secret Fire,
wielder of the flame of Anor.

1399
02:26:30,282 --> 02:26:34,025
The dark fire will not avail you,
flame of Udûn!

1400
02:26:44,045 --> 02:26:46,036
Go back to the Shadow.

1401
02:26:53,888 --> 02:26:58,302
You shall not pass!

1402
02:27:25,462 --> 02:27:29,330
BOROMIR: No! No!
-Gandalf!

1403
02:27:37,015 --> 02:27:39,472
Fly, you fools!

1404
02:27:43,605 --> 02:27:45,766
No!

1405
02:27:51,946 --> 02:27:54,107
Aragorn!

1406
02:28:51,339 --> 02:28:54,172
Legolas, get them up.

1407
02:28:58,304 --> 02:29:00,135
Give them a moment, for pity's sake!

1408
02:29:00,306 --> 02:29:03,924
By nightfall, these hills will
be swarming with Orcs.

1409
02:29:04,144 --> 02:29:07,477
We must reach the woods of Lothlórien.

1410
02:29:08,356 --> 02:29:11,689
Come, Boromir. Legolas.
Gimli, get them up.

1411
02:29:13,194 --> 02:29:15,355
On your feet, Sam.

1412
02:29:15,697 --> 02:29:17,187
Frodo?

1413
02:29:19,284 --> 02:29:20,990
Frodo!

1414
02:30:13,505 --> 02:30:16,042
Stay close, young Hobbits!

1415
02:30:16,758 --> 02:30:20,922
They say that a great sorceress
lives in these woods.

1416
02:30:21,137 --> 02:30:23,674
An Elf-witch...

1417
02:30:24,224 --> 02:30:27,091
...of terrible power.

1418
02:30:27,644 --> 02:30:29,851
All who look upon her...

1419
02:30:30,063 --> 02:30:31,849
...fall under her spell.

1420
02:30:32,065 --> 02:30:33,350
FEMALE VOICE:
<i>Frodo!</i>

1421
02:30:35,610 --> 02:30:37,646
And are never seen again.

1422
02:30:37,862 --> 02:30:42,356
FEMALE VOICE: <i>Your coming to us is</i>
<i>as the footsteps of doom.</i>

1423
02:30:42,575 --> 02:30:46,284
<i>You bring great evil here,</i>
<i>Ring-bearer.</i>

1424
02:30:46,454 --> 02:30:48,240
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

1425
02:30:53,545 --> 02:30:59,131
Well, here's one Dwarf
she won't ensnare so easily.

1426
02:30:59,300 --> 02:31:03,885
I have the eyes of a hawk
and the ears of a fox.

1427
02:31:11,563 --> 02:31:16,148
The Dwarf breathes so loud,
we could have shot him in the dark.

1428
02:31:21,322 --> 02:31:23,313
[IN ELVISH]

1429
02:31:24,200 --> 02:31:26,816
[IN ELVISH]

1430
02:31:34,294 --> 02:31:36,580
So much for the legendary courtesy
of the Elves!

1431
02:31:36,754 --> 02:31:38,665
Speak words we can all understand!

1432
02:31:38,840 --> 02:31:43,425
[IN ENGLISH] We have not had dealings
with the Dwarves since the Dark Days.

1433
02:31:43,678 --> 02:31:46,215
And you know what this Dwarf
says to that?

1434
02:31:46,639 --> 02:31:49,802
[SPEAKS IN DWARVISH]

1435
02:31:53,146 --> 02:31:55,102
That was not so courteous.

1436
02:32:01,654 --> 02:32:05,693
You bring great evil with you.

1437
02:32:07,452 --> 02:32:09,659
You can go no further.

1438
02:32:15,793 --> 02:32:19,706
[SPEAKING IN ELVISH]

1439
02:32:46,908 --> 02:32:49,570
Gandalf's death was not in vain.

1440
02:32:50,703 --> 02:32:52,568
Nor would he have you give up hope.

1441
02:32:54,082 --> 02:32:57,415
You carry a heavy burden, Frodo.

1442
02:32:58,294 --> 02:33:01,411
Don't carry the weight of the dead.

1443
02:33:04,384 --> 02:33:06,420
You will follow me.

1444
02:33:18,106 --> 02:33:20,097
Caras Galadhon.

1445
02:33:20,733 --> 02:33:23,691
The heart of Elvendom on earth.

1446
02:33:23,861 --> 02:33:29,527
Realm of the Lord Celeborn
and of Galadriel, Lady of Light.

1447
02:34:48,529 --> 02:34:51,646
The enemy knows you have entered here.

1448
02:34:52,325 --> 02:34:57,490
What hope you had in secrecy
is now gone.

1449
02:34:59,207 --> 02:35:03,667
Eight there are here, yet nine there
were set out from Rivendell.

1450
02:35:03,920 --> 02:35:05,706
Tell me, where is Gandalf?

1451
02:35:05,922 --> 02:35:09,039
For I much desire to speak with him.

1452
02:35:09,217 --> 02:35:12,004
I can no longer see him from afar.

1453
02:35:12,887 --> 02:35:18,052
GALADRIEL: Gandalf the Grey did not
pass the borders of this land.

1454
02:35:18,309 --> 02:35:20,721
He has fallen into Shadow.

1455
02:35:25,441 --> 02:35:29,935
He was taken by both Shadow and flame.

1456
02:35:31,572 --> 02:35:35,315
A Balrog of Morgoth.

1457
02:35:36,035 --> 02:35:39,402
For we went needlessly
into the net of Moria.

1458
02:35:41,541 --> 02:35:44,749
Needless were none of the deeds
of Gandalf in life.

1459
02:35:45,419 --> 02:35:48,707
We do not yet know his full purpose.

1460
02:35:53,469 --> 02:35:57,758
Do not let the great emptiness
of Khazad-dûm fill your heart...

1461
02:35:58,057 --> 02:36:00,389
...Gimli, son of Glóin.

1462
02:36:01,394 --> 02:36:04,932
For the world has grown
full of peril...

1463
02:36:06,399 --> 02:36:09,061
...and in all lands...

1464
02:36:09,235 --> 02:36:12,727
...love is now mingled with grief.

1465
02:36:25,376 --> 02:36:28,083
What now becomes of this Fellowship?

1466
02:36:28,629 --> 02:36:31,621
Without Gandalf, hope is lost.

1467
02:36:34,594 --> 02:36:37,882
The quest stands upon the edge
of a knife.

1468
02:36:38,055 --> 02:36:41,138
Stray but a little and it will fail...

1469
02:36:41,893 --> 02:36:44,726
...to the ruin of all.

1470
02:36:49,066 --> 02:36:54,902
Yet hope remains
while the Company is true.

1471
02:36:56,449 --> 02:37:01,159
Do not let your hearts be troubled.
Go now and rest...

1472
02:37:01,621 --> 02:37:05,284
...for you are weary with sorrow
and much toil.

1473
02:37:07,543 --> 02:37:09,659
Tonight, you will sleep....

1474
02:37:09,837 --> 02:37:13,250
GALADRIEL:
<i>Welcome, Frodo of the Shire...</i>

1475
02:37:14,842 --> 02:37:16,628
<i>...one who has seen the Eye!</i>

1476
02:37:19,138 --> 02:37:22,005
[SINGING IN ELVISH]

1477
02:37:31,275 --> 02:37:33,857
A lament for Gandalf.

1478
02:37:41,118 --> 02:37:42,654
What do they say about him?

1479
02:37:42,870 --> 02:37:45,532
I have not the heart to tell you.

1480
02:37:48,292 --> 02:37:50,533
For me, the grief is still too near.

1481
02:37:53,506 --> 02:37:56,339
I bet they don't mention his fireworks.

1482
02:37:56,509 --> 02:37:59,546
There should be a verse about them.

1483
02:38:03,099 --> 02:38:05,090
<i>The finest rockets ever seen</i>

1484
02:38:06,227 --> 02:38:09,060
<i>They burst in stars of blue and green</i>

1485
02:38:09,981 --> 02:38:13,394
<i>Or after thunder, silver showers</i>

1486
02:38:13,651 --> 02:38:15,687
[GIMLI SNORES]

1487
02:38:15,903 --> 02:38:18,690
<i>Came falling like a rain of flowers</i>

1488
02:38:18,864 --> 02:38:22,732
Oh, that doesn't do them justice
by a long road.

1489
02:38:33,587 --> 02:38:36,249
ARAGORN:
Take some rest.

1490
02:38:36,424 --> 02:38:39,131
These borders are well-protected.

1491
02:38:39,343 --> 02:38:41,880
I will find no rest here.

1492
02:38:44,724 --> 02:38:47,716
I heard her voice inside my head.

1493
02:38:47,935 --> 02:38:51,678
She spoke of my father
and the fall of Gondor.

1494
02:38:51,897 --> 02:38:57,358
She said to me,
"Even now there is hope left."

1495
02:38:58,738 --> 02:39:01,571
But I cannot see it.

1496
02:39:02,908 --> 02:39:05,399
It is long since we had any hope.

1497
02:39:15,588 --> 02:39:17,704
My father is a noble man.

1498
02:39:18,466 --> 02:39:20,707
But his rule is failing...

1499
02:39:21,052 --> 02:39:26,467
...and our people lose faith.

1500
02:39:27,892 --> 02:39:31,430
He looks to me to make things right,
and I would do it.

1501
02:39:31,604 --> 02:39:35,142
I would see the glory
of Gondor restored.

1502
02:39:37,985 --> 02:39:40,977
Have you ever seen it, Aragorn?

1503
02:39:41,614 --> 02:39:43,650
The White Tower of Ecthelion.

1504
02:39:43,824 --> 02:39:47,658
Glimmering like a spike
of pearl and silver.

1505
02:39:48,329 --> 02:39:51,821
Its banners caught high
in the morning breeze.

1506
02:39:54,710 --> 02:39:56,666
Have you ever been called home...

1507
02:39:56,837 --> 02:40:00,796
...by the clear ringing
of silver trumpets?

1508
02:40:01,425 --> 02:40:04,667
I have seen the White City...

1509
02:40:05,012 --> 02:40:06,502
...long ago.

1510
02:40:07,473 --> 02:40:12,433
One day, our paths will lead us there.

1511
02:40:13,354 --> 02:40:16,312
And the tower guard
shall take up the call:

1512
02:40:16,774 --> 02:40:20,107
"The Lords of Gondor have returned."

1513
02:41:27,303 --> 02:41:29,840
Will you look into the mirror?

1514
02:41:30,014 --> 02:41:31,550
What will I see?

1515
02:41:34,518 --> 02:41:36,850
Even the wisest cannot tell.

1516
02:41:37,771 --> 02:41:39,602
For the mirror...

1517
02:41:39,815 --> 02:41:42,352
...shows many things.

1518
02:41:45,362 --> 02:41:47,728
Things that were...

1519
02:41:47,948 --> 02:41:50,530
...things that are...

1520
02:41:51,285 --> 02:41:53,241
...and some things...

1521
02:41:56,832 --> 02:42:00,120
...that have not yet come to pass.

1522
02:43:04,024 --> 02:43:06,515
[VOICES SPEAKING IN BLACK SPEECH]

1523
02:43:22,710 --> 02:43:25,543
I know what it is you saw.

1524
02:43:27,965 --> 02:43:30,456
For it is also in my mind.

1525
02:43:32,219 --> 02:43:36,303
<i>It is what will come to pass</i>
<i>if you should fail.</i>

1526
02:43:38,684 --> 02:43:43,553
<i>The Fellowship is breaking.</i>
<i>It is already begun.</i>

1527
02:43:44,189 --> 02:43:47,477
<i>He will try to take the Ring.</i>

1528
02:43:47,693 --> 02:43:49,684
<i>You know of whom I speak.</i>

1529
02:43:50,696 --> 02:43:55,360
<i>One by one, it will destroy them all.</i>

1530
02:43:56,869 --> 02:43:59,326
FRODO:
<i>If you ask it of me...</i>

1531
02:43:59,705 --> 02:44:02,742
<i>...I will give you the One Ring.</i>

1532
02:44:03,834 --> 02:44:05,995
You offer it to me freely.

1533
02:44:10,591 --> 02:44:14,504
I do not deny that my heart
has greatly desired this.

1534
02:44:20,893 --> 02:44:24,181
In place of a Dark Lord,
you would have a queen...

1535
02:44:24,605 --> 02:44:28,439
...not dark but beautiful,
and terrible as the dawn!

1536
02:44:29,068 --> 02:44:32,105
Treacherous as the sea!

1537
02:44:32,613 --> 02:44:37,528
Stronger than the foundations
of the earth!

1538
02:44:37,993 --> 02:44:40,359
All shall love me...

1539
02:44:40,579 --> 02:44:43,412
...and despair.

1540
02:44:57,513 --> 02:45:01,802
I pass the test. I will diminish...

1541
02:45:02,101 --> 02:45:04,558
...and go into the West...

1542
02:45:04,770 --> 02:45:09,230
-...and remain Galadriel.
-I cannot do this alone.

1543
02:45:12,820 --> 02:45:16,984
You are a Ring-bearer, Frodo.
To bear a Ring of Power...

1544
02:45:17,908 --> 02:45:19,398
...is to be alone.

1545
02:45:22,746 --> 02:45:25,488
This is Nenya,
the Ring of Adamant.

1546
02:45:25,666 --> 02:45:27,281
And I am its keeper.

1547
02:45:30,504 --> 02:45:34,122
This task was appointed to you.

1548
02:45:35,175 --> 02:45:38,042
And if you do not find a way...

1549
02:45:39,263 --> 02:45:41,254
...no one will.

1550
02:45:41,640 --> 02:45:44,803
Then I know what I must do.

1551
02:45:45,477 --> 02:45:46,683
It's just...

1552
02:45:49,940 --> 02:45:52,181
...I'm afraid to do it.

1553
02:45:55,696 --> 02:46:00,816
Even the smallest person can change
the course of the future.

1554
02:46:06,165 --> 02:46:11,876
Do you know how the Orcs
first came into being?

1555
02:46:12,671 --> 02:46:16,004
They were Elves once.

1556
02:46:17,176 --> 02:46:20,509
Taken by the Dark Powers...

1557
02:46:20,721 --> 02:46:23,884
...tortured and mutilated.

1558
02:46:24,224 --> 02:46:29,514
A ruined and terrible form of life.

1559
02:46:29,813 --> 02:46:31,644
And now...

1560
02:46:33,108 --> 02:46:34,973
...perfected.

1561
02:46:35,694 --> 02:46:38,857
My fighting Uruk-hai...

1562
02:46:40,824 --> 02:46:43,156
...whom do you serve?

1563
02:46:43,368 --> 02:46:45,859
Saruman!

1564
02:47:06,725 --> 02:47:10,183
Hunt them down. Do not stop
until they are found.

1565
02:47:10,395 --> 02:47:13,262
You do not know pain.
You do not know fear.

1566
02:47:13,524 --> 02:47:16,436
You will taste Man-flesh!

1567
02:47:21,532 --> 02:47:25,241
One of the halflings carries
something of great value.

1568
02:47:25,410 --> 02:47:29,574
Bring them to me alive and unspoiled.

1569
02:47:31,416 --> 02:47:32,701
Kill the others.

1570
02:47:51,895 --> 02:47:57,310
CELEBORN: Never before have we clad
strangers in the garb of our own people.

1571
02:47:58,443 --> 02:48:02,277
May these cloaks help shield you
from unfriendly eyes.

1572
02:48:09,454 --> 02:48:10,990
Lembas.

1573
02:48:11,248 --> 02:48:12,829
Elvish waybread.

1574
02:48:15,335 --> 02:48:18,327
One small bite is enough to fill
the stomach of a grown man.

1575
02:48:24,845 --> 02:48:26,801
How many did you eat?

1576
02:48:26,972 --> 02:48:28,633
Four.

1577
02:48:30,142 --> 02:48:33,179
[BELCHES]

1578
02:48:34,438 --> 02:48:37,020
CELEBORN: <i>Every league you travel south,</i>
<i>the danger will increase.</i>

1579
02:48:37,232 --> 02:48:41,350
<i>Mordor Orcs now hold the eastern shore</i>
<i>of the Anduin.</i>

1580
02:48:41,528 --> 02:48:44,019
<i>Nor will you find safety</i>
<i>on the western bank.</i>

1581
02:48:44,239 --> 02:48:48,027
Strange creatures bearing the White Hand
have been seen on our borders.

1582
02:48:48,243 --> 02:48:53,328
Seldom do Orcs journey in the open
under the sun, yet these have done so.

1583
02:49:02,007 --> 02:49:04,544
[IN ELVISH]

1584
02:49:05,927 --> 02:49:07,258
[IN ENGLISH]
By river you have the chance...

1585
02:49:07,429 --> 02:49:10,637
...of outrunning the enemy
to the Falls of Rauros.

1586
02:49:27,908 --> 02:49:32,743
GALADRIEL: My gift for you, Legolas,
is a bow of the Galadhrim.

1587
02:49:32,996 --> 02:49:36,488
Worthy of the skill
of our woodland kin.

1588
02:49:41,880 --> 02:49:44,337
These are the daggers of the Noldorin.

1589
02:49:44,508 --> 02:49:48,501
They have already seen service in war.

1590
02:49:48,679 --> 02:49:50,920
Do not fear, young Peregrin Took.

1591
02:49:51,098 --> 02:49:54,431
<i>You will find your courage.</i>

1592
02:49:56,311 --> 02:49:58,267
<i>And for you, Samwise Gamgee...</i>

1593
02:49:58,438 --> 02:50:01,020
...Elven rope made of hithlain.

1594
02:50:01,191 --> 02:50:03,307
Thank you, my lady.

1595
02:50:05,112 --> 02:50:08,445
Have you run out
of those nice, shiny daggers?

1596
02:50:14,913 --> 02:50:17,950
And what gift would a dwarf ask
of the Elves?

1597
02:50:18,125 --> 02:50:20,241
Nothing.

1598
02:50:20,877 --> 02:50:24,210
Except to look upon the lady
of the Galadhrim one last time...

1599
02:50:24,840 --> 02:50:30,051
...for she is more fair
than all the jewels beneath the earth.

1600
02:50:37,102 --> 02:50:38,638
Actually....

1601
02:50:38,854 --> 02:50:40,469
There was one thing.

1602
02:50:41,314 --> 02:50:43,976
No, no, I'm talking nonsense.
It's quite impossible.

1603
02:50:44,151 --> 02:50:46,938
<i>Stupid to ask.</i>

1604
02:50:49,489 --> 02:50:51,605
GALADRIEL:
<i>I have nothing greater to give...</i>

1605
02:50:51,783 --> 02:50:55,367
...than the gift you already bear.

1606
02:50:56,580 --> 02:50:57,615
[IN ELVISH]

1607
02:50:58,999 --> 02:51:04,244
[IN ELVISH]

1608
02:51:05,005 --> 02:51:08,338
[IN ELVISH]

1609
02:51:09,968 --> 02:51:12,880
[IN ELVISH]

1610
02:51:14,890 --> 02:51:19,600
[IN ELVISH]

1611
02:51:21,021 --> 02:51:24,104
[IN ENGLISH]
That choice is yet before her.

1612
02:51:24,691 --> 02:51:27,603
You have your own choice to make,
Aragorn.

1613
02:51:27,944 --> 02:51:33,780
To rise above the height of all
your fathers since the days of Elendil...

1614
02:51:33,950 --> 02:51:38,284
...or to fall into darkness
with all that is left of your kin.

1615
02:51:45,462 --> 02:51:46,793
[IN ELVISH]

1616
02:51:50,675 --> 02:51:54,042
[IN ELVISH]

1617
02:52:00,560 --> 02:52:01,845
[IN ELVISH]

1618
02:52:01,937 --> 02:52:03,393
[IN ELVISH]

1619
02:52:05,857 --> 02:52:09,065
[IN ENGLISH]
<i>Farewell, Frodo Baggins.</i>

1620
02:52:09,236 --> 02:52:12,649
I give you the light of Eärendil...

1621
02:52:13,406 --> 02:52:15,738
...our most beloved star.

1622
02:52:24,876 --> 02:52:29,245
<i>May it be a light for you</i>
<i>in dark places...</i>

1623
02:52:29,506 --> 02:52:33,590
<i>...when all other lights go out.</i>

1624
02:52:42,435 --> 02:52:45,598
GIMLI: I have taken my worst wound
at this parting...

1625
02:52:46,231 --> 02:52:50,520
...having looked my last upon that
which is fairest.

1626
02:52:51,278 --> 02:52:54,611
Henceforth I will call nothing fair
unless it be her gift to me.

1627
02:52:54,865 --> 02:52:56,776
What was her gift?

1628
02:52:56,992 --> 02:53:01,907
I asked her for one hair
from her golden head.

1629
02:53:02,706 --> 02:53:05,573
She gave me three.

1630
02:54:11,107 --> 02:54:14,520
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

1631
02:54:47,727 --> 02:54:51,185
Gollum. He has tracked us since Moria.

1632
02:54:54,901 --> 02:54:58,018
I had hoped we would lose him
on the river.

1633
02:54:58,238 --> 02:55:01,401
But he's too clever a waterman.

1634
02:55:02,242 --> 02:55:05,575
And if he alerts the enemy
to our whereabouts...

1635
02:55:05,745 --> 02:55:07,986
...it will make the crossing
even more dangerous.

1636
02:55:08,164 --> 02:55:10,246
SAM:
Have some food, Mr. Frodo.

1637
02:55:10,417 --> 02:55:13,500
-No, Sam.
-You haven't eaten anything all day.

1638
02:55:13,670 --> 02:55:16,753
You're not sleeping, neither.
Don't think I haven't noticed.

1639
02:55:17,716 --> 02:55:20,708
-Mr. Frodo--
-I'm all right.

1640
02:55:20,885 --> 02:55:22,045
But you're not.

1641
02:55:22,345 --> 02:55:24,836
I'm here to help you.

1642
02:55:25,015 --> 02:55:26,721
I promised Gandalf that I would.

1643
02:55:32,689 --> 02:55:35,431
You can't help me, Sam.

1644
02:55:37,569 --> 02:55:39,275
Not this time.

1645
02:55:42,198 --> 02:55:44,280
Get some sleep.

1646
02:55:50,540 --> 02:55:52,747
Minas Tirith is the safer road.

1647
02:55:53,293 --> 02:55:56,035
You know that.
From there we can regroup.

1648
02:55:56,713 --> 02:55:58,954
Strike out for Mordor from a place
of strength.

1649
02:55:59,299 --> 02:56:02,166
There is no strength in Gondor
that can avail us.

1650
02:56:02,635 --> 02:56:04,626
You were quick enough to trust
the Elves.

1651
02:56:06,473 --> 02:56:09,306
Have you so little faith
in your own people?

1652
02:56:09,476 --> 02:56:12,468
Yes, there is weakness.
There is frailty.

1653
02:56:12,687 --> 02:56:15,975
But there is courage also,
and honor to be found in Men.

1654
02:56:16,232 --> 02:56:18,439
But you will not see that.

1655
02:56:18,777 --> 02:56:20,187
You are afraid!

1656
02:56:20,445 --> 02:56:22,982
All your life, you have hidden
in the shadows.

1657
02:56:23,281 --> 02:56:26,739
Scared of who you are,
of what you are.

1658
02:56:29,162 --> 02:56:33,496
I will not lead the Ring within
a hundred leagues of your city.

1659
02:56:45,345 --> 02:56:46,710
Frodo.

1660
02:56:48,598 --> 02:56:50,088
The Argonath.

1661
02:56:53,520 --> 02:56:57,263
Long have I desired
to look upon the kings of old.

1662
02:56:58,024 --> 02:56:59,935
My kin.

1663
02:58:18,938 --> 02:58:21,099
We cross the lake at nightfall.

1664
02:58:21,357 --> 02:58:23,939
Hide the boats and continue on foot.

1665
02:58:24,110 --> 02:58:27,602
-We approach Mordor from the North.
-Oh, yes?

1666
02:58:28,031 --> 02:58:31,865
Just a simple matter of finding
our way through Emyn Muil...

1667
02:58:32,035 --> 02:58:35,277
...an impassable labyrinth
of razor-sharp rocks.

1668
02:58:35,455 --> 02:58:38,572
And after that, it gets even better.

1669
02:58:38,958 --> 02:58:43,918
Festering, stinking marshland
as far as the eye can see.

1670
02:58:44,088 --> 02:58:45,453
That is our road.

1671
02:58:47,050 --> 02:58:50,258
I suggest you take some rest
and recover your strength, Master Dwarf.

1672
02:58:50,470 --> 02:58:52,210
Recover my--

1673
02:58:55,225 --> 02:58:57,216
-We should leave now.
-No.

1674
02:58:57,393 --> 02:59:01,853
Orcs patrol the eastern shore.
We must wait for cover of darkness.

1675
02:59:02,065 --> 02:59:05,478
It is not the eastern shore
that worries me.

1676
02:59:05,735 --> 02:59:09,728
A shadow and a threat
has been growing in my mind.

1677
02:59:10,240 --> 02:59:14,404
Something draws near.
I can feel it.

1678
02:59:16,412 --> 02:59:21,372
Recover strength?
Pay no heed to that, young Hobbit.

1679
02:59:21,876 --> 02:59:23,582
Where's Frodo?

1680
02:59:49,195 --> 02:59:51,106
BOROMIR:
None of us should wander alone.

1681
02:59:52,532 --> 02:59:54,614
You, least of all.

1682
02:59:54,826 --> 02:59:57,283
So much depends on you.

1683
02:59:58,329 --> 03:00:00,285
Frodo?

1684
03:00:07,422 --> 03:00:09,959
I know why you seek solitude.

1685
03:00:10,675 --> 03:00:14,133
You suffer. I see it day by day.

1686
03:00:14,929 --> 03:00:17,966
You sure you do not suffer needlessly?

1687
03:00:19,559 --> 03:00:22,175
There are other ways, Frodo.

1688
03:00:22,437 --> 03:00:26,225
-Other paths that we might take.
-I know what you would say.

1689
03:00:26,482 --> 03:00:30,225
It would seem like wisdom
but for the warning in my heart.

1690
03:00:30,486 --> 03:00:33,569
Warning? Against what?

1691
03:00:33,740 --> 03:00:35,856
We're all afraid, Frodo.

1692
03:00:36,075 --> 03:00:39,693
But to let that fear drive us,
to destroy what hope we have...

1693
03:00:39,954 --> 03:00:43,697
-...don't you see that is madness?
-There is no other way.

1694
03:00:45,501 --> 03:00:48,834
I ask only for the strength
to defend my people!

1695
03:00:50,381 --> 03:00:52,463
-If you would but lend me the Ring.
-No.

1696
03:00:53,676 --> 03:00:57,339
-Why do you recoil? I am no thief.
-You are not yourself.

1697
03:00:59,182 --> 03:01:02,515
What chance do you think you have?

1698
03:01:02,685 --> 03:01:07,349
They will find you.
They will take the Ring.

1699
03:01:07,607 --> 03:01:11,270
And you will beg for death
before the end!

1700
03:01:13,404 --> 03:01:15,520
You fool!

1701
03:01:15,698 --> 03:01:19,691
It is not yours, save by unhappy chance!
It could have been mine.

1702
03:01:19,869 --> 03:01:22,702
It should be mine! Give it to me!

1703
03:01:22,872 --> 03:01:24,203
-Give it to me!
-No!

1704
03:01:24,374 --> 03:01:26,205
-Give it to me!
-No.

1705
03:01:33,883 --> 03:01:35,874
I see your mind.

1706
03:01:36,135 --> 03:01:39,047
You will take the Ring to Sauron!

1707
03:01:39,263 --> 03:01:41,128
You will betray us!

1708
03:01:41,391 --> 03:01:44,554
You'll go to your death,
and the death of us all!

1709
03:01:45,019 --> 03:01:48,637
Curse you!
Curse you and all the halflings!

1710
03:01:55,738 --> 03:01:57,228
Frodo?

1711
03:02:01,577 --> 03:02:03,158
Frodo.

1712
03:02:07,083 --> 03:02:09,074
What have I done?

1713
03:02:09,293 --> 03:02:11,033
Please, Frodo.

1714
03:02:11,254 --> 03:02:13,916
Frodo, I'm sorry!

1715
03:02:14,132 --> 03:02:15,997
Frodo!

1716
03:02:41,284 --> 03:02:44,617
[VOICE OF THE RING
SPEAKS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1717
03:03:02,472 --> 03:03:03,882
Frodo?

1718
03:03:05,141 --> 03:03:08,224
-It has taken Boromir.
-Where is the Ring?

1719
03:03:08,478 --> 03:03:10,218
Stay away!

1720
03:03:10,646 --> 03:03:12,227
Frodo!

1721
03:03:14,484 --> 03:03:18,318
-I swore to protect you.
-Can you protect me from yourself?

1722
03:03:27,997 --> 03:03:30,488
Would you destroy it?

1723
03:03:35,505 --> 03:03:37,416
VOICE OF THE RING:
<i>Aragorn.</i>

1724
03:03:40,843 --> 03:03:43,175
<i>Aragorn.</i>

1725
03:03:45,014 --> 03:03:46,845
<i>Elessar.</i>

1726
03:03:54,524 --> 03:03:57,857
I would have gone with you to the end.

1727
03:03:58,528 --> 03:04:01,361
Into the very fires of Mordor.

1728
03:04:04,700 --> 03:04:05,860
I know.

1729
03:04:08,371 --> 03:04:13,786
Look after the others. Especially Sam.
He will not understand.

1730
03:04:17,547 --> 03:04:19,287
Go, Frodo!

1731
03:04:22,301 --> 03:04:23,791
Run.

1732
03:04:24,053 --> 03:04:25,714
Run!

1733
03:04:50,246 --> 03:04:51,907
Mr. Frodo!

1734
03:05:01,215 --> 03:05:02,955
Find the halfling!

1735
03:05:04,594 --> 03:05:07,131
Find the halfling!

1736
03:05:10,600 --> 03:05:12,261
Elendil!

1737
03:05:18,774 --> 03:05:20,355
Aragorn, go!

1738
03:05:42,048 --> 03:05:43,379
PIPPIN:
Frodo!

1739
03:05:43,966 --> 03:05:45,547
Hide here. Quick!

1740
03:05:46,177 --> 03:05:47,633
Come on!

1741
03:05:50,139 --> 03:05:52,130
What's he doing?

1742
03:05:56,395 --> 03:05:58,386
He's leaving.

1743
03:06:03,152 --> 03:06:06,064
-No!
-Pippin!

1744
03:06:10,993 --> 03:06:13,325
MERRY:
Run, Frodo. Go on!

1745
03:06:13,913 --> 03:06:16,996
-Hey! Hey, you!
-Over here!

1746
03:06:17,416 --> 03:06:18,997
-Over here!
-This way!

1747
03:06:29,845 --> 03:06:32,177
-It's working!
-I know it's working! Run!

1748
03:07:25,651 --> 03:07:27,266
[HORN BLOWS]

1749
03:07:27,570 --> 03:07:30,607
-The horn of Gondor.
-Boromir.

1750
03:08:13,699 --> 03:08:14,814
Run!

1751
03:09:51,589 --> 03:09:54,001
[ARROW HITS]

1752
03:11:46,412 --> 03:11:48,027
No.

1753
03:11:51,875 --> 03:11:54,912
-They took the little ones.
-Hold still.

1754
03:11:55,254 --> 03:11:57,336
Frodo. Where is Frodo?

1755
03:11:59,216 --> 03:12:00,626
I let Frodo go.

1756
03:12:01,343 --> 03:12:03,925
Then you did what I could not.

1757
03:12:04,930 --> 03:12:08,263
I tried to take the Ring from him.

1758
03:12:08,767 --> 03:12:13,056
-The Ring is beyond our reach now.
-Forgive me.

1759
03:12:13,272 --> 03:12:15,558
I did not see it.

1760
03:12:15,774 --> 03:12:18,937
-I have failed you all.
-No, Boromir.

1761
03:12:19,403 --> 03:12:21,940
You fought bravely.

1762
03:12:22,239 --> 03:12:24,901
You have kept your honor.

1763
03:12:25,451 --> 03:12:27,407
BOROMIR:
Leave it.

1764
03:12:27,745 --> 03:12:29,781
It is over.

1765
03:12:30,956 --> 03:12:36,246
The world of Men will fall.
And all will come to darkness...

1766
03:12:36,670 --> 03:12:39,662
...and my city to ruin.

1767
03:12:43,761 --> 03:12:46,468
I do not know what strength
is in my blood...

1768
03:12:46,638 --> 03:12:50,631
...but I swear to you,
I will not let the White City fall...

1769
03:12:51,643 --> 03:12:54,134
...nor our people fail.

1770
03:12:55,147 --> 03:12:56,478
Our people.

1771
03:13:00,319 --> 03:13:02,435
Our people.

1772
03:13:24,176 --> 03:13:27,168
I would have followed you, my brother.

1773
03:13:28,722 --> 03:13:30,713
My captain.

1774
03:13:33,352 --> 03:13:35,308
My king.

1775
03:13:54,957 --> 03:13:57,198
Be at peace...

1776
03:13:57,543 --> 03:13:59,534
...son of Gondor.

1777
03:14:16,061 --> 03:14:19,394
They will look for his coming
from the White Tower.

1778
03:14:19,898 --> 03:14:22,890
But he will not return.

1779
03:14:46,091 --> 03:14:48,082
Frodo!

1780
03:15:07,571 --> 03:15:10,813
FRODO:
<i>I wish the Ring had never come to me.</i>

1781
03:15:12,117 --> 03:15:15,109
<i>I wish none of this had happened.</i>

1782
03:15:18,081 --> 03:15:20,823
GANDALF: <i>So do all who live</i>
<i>to see such times...</i>

1783
03:15:21,043 --> 03:15:24,456
<i>...but that is not for them to decide.</i>

1784
03:15:24,630 --> 03:15:27,292
<i>All you have to decide...</i>

1785
03:15:27,549 --> 03:15:32,293
...is what to do with the time
that is given to you.

1786
03:16:01,124 --> 03:16:03,160
Frodo, no!

1787
03:16:03,669 --> 03:16:05,000
Frodo!

1788
03:16:05,837 --> 03:16:08,499
-Mr. Frodo!
-No, Sam.

1789
03:16:12,010 --> 03:16:14,001
Go back, Sam!

1790
03:16:14,513 --> 03:16:18,097
-I'm going to Mordor alone.
-Of course you are.

1791
03:16:18,308 --> 03:16:21,141
And I'm coming with you!

1792
03:16:21,603 --> 03:16:24,015
You can't swim!

1793
03:16:27,818 --> 03:16:29,524
Sam!

1794
03:16:35,117 --> 03:16:36,402
Sam!

1795
03:17:17,367 --> 03:17:20,074
I made a promise, Mr. Frodo.

1796
03:17:20,412 --> 03:17:24,746
A promise:
"Don't you leave him, Samwise Gamgee."

1797
03:17:25,876 --> 03:17:28,458
And I don't mean to.

1798
03:17:28,754 --> 03:17:30,915
I don't mean to.

1799
03:17:32,591 --> 03:17:34,422
Sam.

1800
03:17:49,274 --> 03:17:50,935
Come on.

1801
03:18:19,429 --> 03:18:23,968
Hurry! Frodo and Sam
have reached the eastern shore.

1802
03:18:38,824 --> 03:18:43,818
-You mean not to follow them.
-Frodo's fate is no longer in our hands.

1803
03:18:47,290 --> 03:18:52,159
Then it has all been in vain.
The Fellowship has failed.

1804
03:19:04,015 --> 03:19:07,178
Not if we hold true to each other.

1805
03:19:08,520 --> 03:19:13,014
We will not abandon Merry and Pippin
to torment and death.

1806
03:19:14,025 --> 03:19:19,270
Not while we have strength left.
Leave all that can be spared behind.

1807
03:19:20,532 --> 03:19:22,568
We travel light.

1808
03:19:22,784 --> 03:19:24,695
Let us hunt some Orc.

1809
03:19:27,664 --> 03:19:29,700
Yes!

1810
03:19:48,685 --> 03:19:50,095
FRODO:
Mordor.

1811
03:19:50,729 --> 03:19:54,096
I hope the others find a safer road.

1812
03:19:55,066 --> 03:19:57,603
Strider will look after them.

1813
03:19:58,570 --> 03:20:01,903
I don't suppose
we'll ever see them again.

1814
03:20:02,240 --> 03:20:04,697
We may yet, Mr. Frodo.

1815
03:20:04,910 --> 03:20:06,400
We may.

1816
03:20:08,538 --> 03:20:09,573
Sam...

1817
03:20:13,210 --> 03:20:15,826
...I'm glad you are with me.
